    "refuted": 13,
    "synthesis": "# Synthesis: Index Entry-Creation Plans — Adversarial Review\n\n**Scope:** all entry-creation plans under `plans/` that produced any of the 27 entries in `corpus/index/`, judged against the stated goal — *\"a large and extraordinarily detailed index of every document. Every claim and every clause. Every point of connection and every weakness.\"*\n\n**Verification posture:** 207 plan defects filed; 89 of 93 spot-verified survived refutation. The confirmations carried numeric corrections which are used below in preference to the originals. Seven refutations are material and are reported in §2B; refuted causal claims are not reused as evidence anywhere in this document.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What the current authoring process actually is\n\n### 1.1 The plan lineage\n\nThree generations, in causal order:\n\n| Generation | Plans | Entries produced |\n|---|---|---|\n| **G1 — hand-authored, per-cluster** | `plans/phantasia-cluster-2025-analysis.md` (2026-05-10), `plans/rdr2-secondary-cluster-analysis.md` (2026-06-23), `plans/heidegger-*-analysis.md`, `plans/wendt-design-for-dasein-analysis.md`, `plans/grammar-of-motives-burke-1945-analysis.md` | Phantasia Secondary, RDR2 Secondary, BT, BCAP, FCM, Wendt, Grammar, Uncomfortable, Uexküll, Rickert |\n| **G2 — the gold-standard instance** | `plans/boredom-secondary-cluster-index-plan-2026-07-14.md` (287 lines) | Boredom Secondary (Part III) |\n| **G3 — the canonical template** | `plans/secondary-cluster-index-plan-TEMPLATE-2026-07-15.md` (238 lines), which states at `:4-6` it is *\"Modeled on\"* the Boredom plan and its executed output | Instantiated exactly once, as `plans/vr-pedagogy-secondary-cluster-index-plan-2026-07-15.md` (244 lines) → VR Pedagogy Secondary (Part III) |\n| **off-lineage** | `plans/boredom-experiment-index-entry-plan-2026-07-10.md` (281 l), `-v2-2026-07-11.md` (313 l), `-channel-schema-anchor-plan-2026-07-16.md` (201 l), `plans/new-media-presence-ingestion-phase1-report-2026-07-20.md` | Boredom Experiment, Presence Theory, Social Presence, Rhetoric of Interactivity |\n\n**Chronology matters and was previously mis-stated.** The template *post-dates* Boredom by ~10 hours and post-dates Phantasia/RDR2/Emotion by 22–65 days. It did not cause those entries' defects; it **codified** Boredom's shape and propagated it forward. Its only true instantiation is VR Pedagogy — which drew 36 defects, the most of any entry in the corpus.\n\n### 1.2 The pipeline as practised (template `§5`, `:136-185`)\n\n**Phase −1 — Survey & self-authored spec** (`:49-102`). `pdfinfo` + `md5sum` + `pdftotext -l 3` per file (`:54`); de-dup/haystack rubric (`:57-67`); derive 4–8 \"strands\"; derive the concordance axes (≤15 × ≤15) and the ≤12-type controlled vocabulary; emit a filled cluster spec to `plans/`. → **GATE G0**: present spec, wait for human sign-off (`:102`).\n\n**Phase 0 — Extraction + overview** (`:137-146`). `pdftotext` every source **to the scratchpad** `<scratchpad>/<prefix>-txt/` (`:138`), one `.txt` each; agents get the `.txt` path, never the PDF. Write `phase0-overview.md` and `_synthesis/manifest.json` (`:145`), the latter declared authoritative thereafter (`:78-79`).\n\n**Phase 1 — Per-source metadata** (`:148-150`). One agent per unit, batched ~8. Header fields only.\n\n**Phase 2 — Deep per-source** (`:152-165`). One agent per unit; two-pass on `deep-long`. Each unit emits three files:\n- `.md` — paraphrastic prose, **budgeted in words**: 1,500–3,500 (humanities) / 1,000–2,500 (empirical) / 400–1,000 (map) (`:153-154`); fixed 9-part skeleton; ends with a `\"Not treated:\"` line (`:158`).\n- `.json` — a bag of parallel arrays: `constructs[], measures[], readings[], concepts[], interlocutors[], tensions[], bridges{}` (`:160`). **No element schema.**\n- `-edges.csv` — `source,relation,target,locus,note`; floors map ≥12 / deep ≥20 / deep-long ≥35 (`:162`).\n\n**Phase 3 — Cluster synthesis, authored in the main loop, not by subagents** (`:167-180`). 3A ontology (`#### N. Name` + bullets, `:168-172`); 3B `global-edges.csv` \"concat + dedup\" + debate map (`:173`); 3C concept-matrix + contested readings; 3D concordance + ≥50-lemma terminology appendix (`:176-178`); 3E citation networks + 5 Mermaid graphs + evolution narrative.\n\n**Phase 4 — Cross-pipeline** (`:182-185`). `bridge-sources/anchor-pointers.md`, pointers only; `graph-cross-pipeline-bridge.mmd` capped at ≤25 edges.\n\n**Phase 5 — Compiler wiring, done LAST** (`:187-201`). Back up `compile-corpus-index.py` and `compiled-index.json`; add **one hand-edited dict entry to `TEXT_DIRS`**; run the compiler; \"verify node/term counts by reading (do not assume)\"; \"re-run the repo's verbatim-quote detector\" (`:199` — **this tool does not exist**). → **GATE G1**: show TEXT_DIRS diff + compiled counts + one sample unit trio, wait for sign-off; never commit before G1 (`:200-201`).\n\n**Orchestration** (`:205-214`): budget `1 + N + N`; documented ~1-in-8 subagent no-op rate with the mitigation *\"verify all three files exist on disk for every unit and **self-author any gaps**\"* (`:210`); deviations recorded in `manifest.json → planCorrections` (`:214`).\n\n**Gates** (`:216-229`): eight markdown checkboxes in the plan file. No artifact is emitted. No script exists.\n\n### 1.3 What actually reaches runtime\n\n`scripts/compile-corpus-index.py` opens exactly **two** files per registered entry:\n- `<analysis_subdir>/book-level-ontology.md`, else `cluster-ontology.md` — `collect_ontology_nodes` (~`:1185-1229`), warning only when the file is **missing**, never when it parses to zero nodes;\n- `<analysis_subdir>/tension-edges.json` — `collect_tension_edges` (~`:1254-1273`), requiring `node_a`/`node_b`.\n\n`collect_cross_pipeline_hooks` globs the Aristotle directory only. Nothing else in `corpus/index/` is read by any runtime consumer. Verified output of the whole corpus:\n\n```\ncompiled-index.json: 701 ontologyNodes · 72 crossPipelineHooks · 64 tensionEdges · 1722 canonicalTerms\n```\n\nThe node record carries `name, greek, transliteration, translation, definition, type, units, text, aliases, centralityTier`. **No id. No page. No quote. No locus.**\n\n### 1.4 Cost profile of one entry — VR Pedagogy Secondary, the template's only instantiation\n\n| Input | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Plan authoring | 244 lines + 238-line template |\n| Agent invocations | 1 (main) + 34 (metadata) + 34 (deep) + main-loop Phase 3 = **69 agent-turns minimum**, before retries |\n| Human checkpoints | 2 (G0, G1) |\n| Wall/scope | plan 2026-07-15 → entry 2026-07-16 |\n| **Output on disk** | **201 files / 4,347,691 bytes**; 99,531 words of authored prose; 34 unit trios; 1,131 per-unit edge rows → 1,129 global rows; 94 concordance cells; 79 lemmas; 10 debates; 5 `.mmd` |\n| **Files read by any consumer** | **1** — `_synthesis/cluster-ontology.md`, 34,836 bytes = **0.80% of the entry** |\n| **Records reaching runtime** | **60 ontology nodes, 0 edges** (no `tension-edges.json` exists — the template never names the file) |\n| Addressable records total | ~1,300 → **≈76 authored words per record**; ≈1,659 words per *runtime-addressable* record |\n| Finest locator anywhere | a page number |\n\nBoredom Secondary, same shape: 189 files, 55 units, **1,918** per-unit edge rows → **1,897** global (18 locus-distinct rows silently destroyed across 10 edge keys), 2,924 structured sub-items, 68 authored nodes → **61** compiled (name-merge loss), 1,897 edges → **0** at runtime. Measured source corpus: 563,740 words over 45 PDFs, 463 reading records = **one claim record per ~1,218 source words**, i.e. **~21× coarser** than the Dissertation entry's 1-per-58.\n\n**The economics are the finding.** ~69 agent-turns and ~100k authored words buy 60 name-only nodes. The programme is paying claim-level prices for concept-level delivery.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Plan defect register\n\n### 2A. CONFIRMED defects, most severe first\n\nEach row: **plan instruction → built artifact → observed defect → downstream consequence.**\n\n---\n\n#### D1 — CRITICAL · The plan commissions ~14 synthesis artifacts and wires one\n`TEMPLATE:107-133` (folder layout) + `:187-197` (wiring) · `boredom:119-132, 228-243` · `vr-ped:194-205`\n\n**Instruction:** create 20+ `_synthesis` artifacts and a `.md`/`.json`/`-edges.csv` trio per source; wire by adding **one** `TEXT_DIRS` dict entry with `ontology_format: \"header\"`.\n**Artifact:** VR Pedagogy — 201 files, 4.35 MB.\n**Defect:** the compiler opens one of them (`cluster-ontology.md`, 0.80% of bytes). `global-edges.csv`, all 34 unit `.json`, all 34 `-edges.csv`, the concordance, concept-matrix, debate map, terminology appendix, citation networks and 5 `.mmd` have **no reader anywhere in the repo**. `scripts/normalize-edges.py` — the only script that reads a `global-edges.csv` — has a hardcoded pipeline registry (`:35-42`) containing no cluster.\n**Consequence:** 1,129 edges, 94 concordance cells, 79 lemmas, 10 debate axes, 233 readings → **zero** runtime records. Corpus-wide: ~35 MB under `corpus/index/` compiles to a 664 KB name-only index.\n\n---\n\n#### D2 — CRITICAL · The claim is not a record type anywhere\n`TEMPLATE:127-130, 152-165` · `boredom:203-205` · `vr-ped:179-184`\n\n**Instruction:** the atom is the SOURCE — one folder, one `.md`, one `.json`, one `-edges.csv`, keyed `<PREFIX>NN`. `READING/CLAIM` appears only as an *edge-endpoint vocabulary term* (`boredom:165`), never as an addressable object.\n**Artifact:** claims exist as unnamed array elements at array positions.\n**Defect:** ~7 records per source across 27 entries (355 unit-record files / ~320 distinct units / 372 unit analyses). Target is 50–500.\n**Consequence:** the claim-level material *already written* is unaddressable. VR Pedagogy: 1,277 provenance-tagged assertions in prose vs 233 structured readings (5.5×). Boredom: ~6,300 locus-bearing propositions in 137,928 words of unit `.md` vs 463 readings (13.6×). Aristotle: 973 Bekker-anchored claim bullets, 2,323 Bekker loci with line numbers, zero claim records. **The index programme has been treating an addressing problem as an authoring problem.**\n\n---\n\n#### D3 — CRITICAL · No schema, anywhere\n`TEMPLATE:159-161` · `boredom:204`\n\n**Instruction:** `boredom:204` names seven collection keys and gives per-field guidance for exactly one — `measures` at `:205`, and that guidance is *prose* (\"signal, apparatus, sample N, key result\"), not literal keys. The word \"schema\" appears **0 times** in both the template and the Boredom plan. The one by-reference spec, *\"mirror of the RDR2 unit JSON\"*, points at a precedent that has **no `constructs` and no `measures` keys at all** and whose own arrays are majority bare strings — and `boredom:252` shows the RDR2 exemplar path was never even handed to the executing agents.\n**Artifact:** 55 agents, 55 inventions.\n**Defect:** 2,924 sub-items in **42 mutually incompatible shapes**. `readings[]`: 8 key-signatures. `measures[]`: 7, including a camelCase/snake_case split *inside the one field set the plan specified* (54 `sampleN/keyResult` vs 41 `sample_n/key_result`). `concepts[]` 6 shapes incl. 87 bare strings; `interlocutors[]` 5 incl. 146 bare strings; `tensions[]` 5 incl. 46 bare strings.\n**Built-in control experiment proving causation:** where the plan supplied a **closed value list** (`boredom:147-151`, eleven construct labels), **407 of 425** construct labels (96%) match verbatim across the same 55 agents. Same agents, same session — the only variable is whether the plan specified.\n**Consequence:** propagated to `TEMPLATE:159-161` one day later (\"matching the Boredom precedent\"), producing 23 shapes and bare strings again in VR Pedagogy. 49 schema-violation defects corpus-wide.\n\n---\n\n#### D4 — CRITICAL · `tension-edges.json` — the compiler's only edge channel — is named in no plan\n`TEMPLATE` (0 occurrences) · `boredom:119-132` (absent from the layout) · `vr-ped` (absent from §2/§5/§6/§8)\n\n**Defect:** the file the compiler requires, and the field names it requires (`node_a`/`node_b`), appear in no plan in the lineage. `grep -ni tension` on the template returns exactly one hit — `:160`, a per-unit JSON array name.\n**Consequence:** no template-lineage cluster has one. VR Pedagogy's 98 unit tensions + 10 debate axes → 0 runtime edges. Boredom's 211 tensions + 11 axes → 0. All 64 `tensionEdges` in `compiled-index.json` come from pre-template book entries. And where the file *does* exist, four of eleven yield zero because the key names were never stated: `pole_A/pole_B` (Uncomfortable, 15 lost), `wendt_position/against` (Wendt, 12), `label/description` (In-Game 12, Grammar 16+21).\n**Note:** naming the file is necessary but insufficient — the fix must specify required key names *plus* a post-compile assertion that the new entry's edge count is non-zero.\n\n---\n\n#### D5 — CRITICAL · The blanket 25-word verbatim ban makes the target atom unstorable\n`TEMPLATE:44` (\"all sources are copyrighted secondary literature. **No ≥25-word verbatim quotation anywhere**\"), `:225`, `:212` · `boredom:199, 262` · `vr-ped:31-32, 221`\n\n**Instruction:** paraphrase; ≤12-word anchor phrases with a page number.\n**Defect (i) — granularity.** A clause-level index must store the clause; the clause *is* the verbatim. Nothing in 1,758 files carries a sentence offset, character span or bbox. The finest locator anywhere is a page, a page range, a Bekker line pair, or a video timestamp.\n**Defect (ii) — undifferentiated rights.** One rule binds the user's own dissertation and MA thesis, public-domain Aristotle/Equiano 1789/Radcliffe 1794/Austen 1811/Darwin 1872, and third-party monographs alike.\n**Defect (iii) — no fidelity rule.** The constraint is on *length*, never on *truth*. It makes short quotation maximally likely and entirely unchecked.\n**Consequence:** entries actively destroy evidence to comply. `In-Game .../ig-10-deep.json:434-441` records a `content_filter_audit`: block quotes \"paraphrased\", canonical definitions kept only because \"24-word … under the 25-word ceiling per task constraint\", \"23-word … under ceiling\", \"20-word … under ceiling\". Uncomfortable does the same at `us-03-radcliffe.json:110, :234`. And in VR Pedagogy, **at least four quoted spans in `ped-sec-29` do not occur in the source**, all under source-attributing `FE` tags — `\"sense of being in the place\"` (`:7`, FE p.456-457) against the source's `\"being in the virtual place\"`; `\"sense of being there\"` and `\"sense of being together with another\"` (`:26`) against `\"sense of being together\"` / `\"sense of being with another\"`. Six words, inside the 12-word allowance, undetectable by every gate the plan defines.\n\n---\n\n#### D6 — CRITICAL · \"Compiler runs clean\" is unfalsifiable, and the parse gate measures a marker the parser ignores\n`TEMPLATE:227-228` · `boredom:238-240` · `vr-ped:223`\n\n**Defect (i):** `main()` has no exit-code path and no error accumulation. `parse_header_ontology` returns `[]` for an unparsable file with **no warning**; `collect_ontology_nodes` warns only when the file is *missing*. Zero-yield with zero diagnostics is a passing state.\n**Defect (ii):** the gate checks that `cluster-ontology.md` \"has a parseable `## 3A. Canonical Node List`\". For `ontology_format: \"header\"` the parser splits the **whole file** on `^(?:####\\s+\\d+\\.\\s+|\\*\\*\\d+\\.\\s+)`; only `_parse_header_tables` restricts to 3A, and only for pipe tables. So the gate passes with the heading and zero nodes, and passes with nodes and no heading.\n**Consequence:** four `tension-edges.json` files discard 55 records while the compiler reports success. Three clusters (Phantasia, RDR2 Secondary, Emotion) hold prose-dialect ontologies with **0** `#### N.` matches. *(Refinement, per verification: those three are unregistered, so the zero is counterfactual, and the template is chronologically their remedy, not their cause — see §2B/R1. The compiler facts stand as compiler defects the new plan must route around.)*\n\n---\n\n#### D7 — CRITICAL · Parenthetical qualifiers in node headings poison the corpus-wide term list\n`vr-ped:118-127` (the plan's own canonical labels: `presence (spatial/physical)`, `immersion (technological)`, `IVR (HMD)`, `conventional instruction (control)`) + `:186-187` routing them into `## 3A` · `TEMPLATE:168-172` (\"Replicate the Boredom/FCM structure **exactly**\")\n\n**Instruction:** \"replicate the exemplar\" with no statement of the field grammar.\n**Code:** `_parse_header_section` extracts an end-anchored parenthetical and assigns it to `greek` when no `greek_lemma`/`german_lemma` exists — always true for a non-classical domain. `build_canonical_terms` exports `name`, `transliteration`, `greek` + aliases into the global list. `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:268` greedy-substring-matches any term ≥4 chars for a +0.10 boost, corpus-wide; `:811` injects the list into `protectedTerms`.\n**Defect:** **19 of 60** VR Pedagogy nodes compiled with truncated names and the qualifier in the `greek` slot — `Immersion`/`technological`, `Conventional instruction`/`control`, `SEM process model`/`no media contrast`, `Simulator Sickness Questionnaire`/`SSQ`, and 15 more.\n**Consequence:** the bare English words **`technological`** and **`control`** are live entries in the 1,722-term greedy-match list applied to every query in every registered corpus. Boredom contributed `gaze-based`, `anyone`, `publicness` the same way.\n**Correction to the original finding:** the claim that the Boredom exemplar contained *zero* parentheticals is false — `cluster-ontology.md:367` carries `#### 32. Motivation model (gaze-based)` and is likewise corrupted. The exemplar already contained the breaking form at 1/68; the VR plan's own label list took it to 19/60.\n\n---\n\n#### D8 — CRITICAL · The extraction is written to a scratchpad and is treated as disposable\n`TEMPLATE:138` · `boredom:184-186, 281` · `vr-ped:166-171, 239` (the VR plan *observes* the prior session's extraction did not persist, and still specifies an ephemeral destination)\n\n**Defect:** the `.txt` is the addressing substrate for every locus, every line anchor, every quoted phrase — and is never required to be retained, hashed, or version-pinned. The word \"offset\" appears **0 times** in the template and 0 times in the Boredom plan.\n**Consequence:** `In-Game (Calleja 2011)/` records 995 line-range references (`ig-10-incorporation.json:20` \"Verified directly from `/tmp/calleja-fulltext.txt` lines 5855-6285\"). That file no longer exists. ~1,000 clause-adjacent pointers — the finest addressing in the whole corpus — are unresolvable, and the entry's own falsification notes can no longer be checked. In VR Pedagogy the same policy made the `ped-sec-29` fabrication undiagnosable from the entry's own materials.\n\n---\n\n#### D9 — HIGH · No page-offset model, and no requirement that any locus resolve\n`TEMPLATE:54, 162-165` (loci must \"carry\" page anchors, never resolve) · no plan in the repo requires offset verification\n\n**Consequence:** Aristotle — 33 of 34 unit records carry `pdf_pages` from a superseded linear offset, errors up to 47 pages; `bekker-index` has 101 of 188 loci off by >2 pages. Rickert — `rickert-structured/manifest.json:7` declares `pdf_page_offset: 20`, which is both wrong and **non-constant** (drifts to 15).\n**The correct pattern already exists, outside the lineage:** `Uncomfortable Situations/_synthesis/us-literary-loci-concordance.json` declares `page_offset_rule: \"book p.n = PDF p.n + 10\"` alongside a `tier_rule`; and `Wendt - Design for Dasein` mandated a double locus `(p.NN / pdf NN)` on every citation with measured **307/307 = 100%** compliance. The template abstracted both away.\n\n---\n\n#### D10 — HIGH · \"Concat + dedup\" with no key; the gate counts the post-dedup number\n`TEMPLATE:115, :173` · gated at `:219` / `boredom:259` / `vr-ped:216`\n\n**Defect:** neither the key nor the output columns are stated, and there is no edge id to dedup *on* (`:162` defines no id). Two executions of the identical instruction chose different keys.\n**Measured (corrected):** Boredom keyed `(source,relation,target)` — 1,918 per-unit rows → 1,897, destroying **18 locus-distinct rows across 10 edge keys** (e.g. `bor-sec-12 → bridges-to-fcm → fcm-05` carried four distinct loci; one survives). VR Pedagogy keyed `(source,relation,target,locus)` — 1,131 → 1,129, losing **2 non-duplicate edges with distinct notes**, and five further triples survived only because their loci happened to differ.\n**Perversity:** the gate counts rows *after* dedup, so a more destructive key makes the gate **easier** to pass. 1,897 cleared the 550 floor by 3.4× while 18 evidence rows were being destroyed.\n**Header divergence:** four sibling clusters, four incompatible `global-edges.csv` headers. VR Pedagogy — the template's own child — shipped the per-unit header verbatim as the aggregate header, the only one of 17 with neither a unit nor an edge-id column. And a canonical edge schema four months older already existed in `scripts/normalize-edges.py` (`source,relation,target,domain,confidence,pipeline,units,note` + computed id); the template never cites it and is incompatible with it — the normalizer reads `units|chapter|chapters|works`, never `unit`, and never reads `locus` at all, so the sole page anchor on every template-lineage edge is dropped on normalization while `confidence` is fabricated as `\"medium\"`.\n\n---\n\n#### D11 — HIGH · No id grammar below the unit, and no uniqueness rule at any level\n`boredom:101-106` (unit ids only) · `TEMPLATE:73` · \"unique\"/\"namespace\"/\"collision\" appear 0 times in either plan\n\n**Consequence (corrected upward):** 9 of 55 Boredom agents invented sub-unit ids; **42 distinct id values collide across 8 units** — `C1`–`C9` six ways, `DA1`–`DA3` **eight** ways, `F1`–`F15` two ways. The 46 units that complied left **296 readings permanently unaddressable**. Wendt: 91 of 139 claim objects have no id, 20 collide. Uncomfortable carries **two disjoint concept registries in one directory** (`concept-matrix.csv` `C-US-01..40` vs `book-level-ontology.json` `US-C-001..036`). Four Boredom agents reached for sub-unit subjects the plan denied them and put section markers in the edge CSV subject column — **119 global-edge rows** whose subject is `§4`, `§2`, `n.8`, `Intro`.\n**Compounding at the compiler:** `deduplicate_ontology_nodes` merges globally on `name.lower()` and picks the longest definition; 20 fused rows now concatenate provenance across entries (`\"Boredom Secondary (Part III); Heidegger - Being and Time; Heidegger - FCM\"`). No compiled node carries an id at all; the only address for any runtime node is its display string.\n\n---\n\n#### D12 — HIGH · Cross-entry relation targets are free text unless the plan enumerates them\n`boredom:170-171` vs `boredom:24`\n\n**The plan contains its own control.** `bridges-to-fcm`, whose target ids are enumerated literally at `:24`, resolves **68/68 = 100%**. `grounds-measure`, described only in prose, resolves **0/37** across 27 free-text strings, while the target entry exists on disk with five stable ids `bex-00..bex-04` and not one edge names any of them. `bridges-to-part-iii`: 128 edges, 122 distinct targets, 118 singletons (92%). `boredom:252-253` instructs the orchestrator to hand each agent \"the dataset channel list\" — a list the plan never provides in its 287 lines.\n**Consequence:** 44 dangling-reference defects corpus-wide.\n\n---\n\n#### D13 — HIGH · Gate results are never emitted as an artifact\n`TEMPLATE:216-229` · `boredom:256-265` · `vr-ped:213-224` — all markdown checkboxes inside the plan file\n\n**Consequence:** only **2 of 27** entries have a `quality-gates-report.md` (Wendt, RDR2 Secondary) and **neither is template-built**; only 1 has machine-readable metrics. The template also abstracted away artifacts its own precedents produced unbidden: Phantasia's `_synthesis/render-validation.txt` (mmdc version, per-graph node/edge counts, PASS table) and RDR2's gate table with its explicit *\"Gates NOT fully met (reported honestly)\"* section. Neither Boredom nor VR Pedagogy produced either. VLE's own manifest records the terminal form of the disease: `\"phase-3 registration build … gates deferred to post-run review\"` — the review never happened, and 7 of 18 VLE nodes now serve superseded figures to runtime.\n\n---\n\n#### D14 — HIGH · Word budgets are the only volume instruction, and they compete with extraction\n`TEMPLATE:153-154` · `boredom:198-199` (bands stated in Phase 2, gated nowhere)\n\n**Consequence:** 18 of 55 Boredom units violate the bands; **17 of the 18 overshoot** (bor-sec-52 at 4,216w against a 3,500 cap; bor-sec-25 at 3,439w against 2,500). The overshoot is the measurable signature of the granularity ceiling: analysts wrote into prose what the JSON had nowhere to hold. Meanwhile three units ship **zero** readings while carrying 1,302–2,581 words of analysis, and pass every gate.\n\n---\n\n#### D15 — HIGH · \"Self-author any gaps\" institutionalises unmarked fabrication\n`TEMPLATE:8-10` (cheap model, do not stall, `****** UNVERIFIED:` escape) + `:208-210` (self-author) · `boredom:249-251` · `vr-ped:210-211`\n\n**Defect:** completeness is defined as *file existence*. A main-loop stand-in authored **without the source in context** is indistinguishable from an agent-read unit, and no `derivation` field exists to mark it.\n**Consequence:** 55/55 and 34/34 trios \"complete\" while readings range 0–30 and measures 0–12; no record anywhere of which units were self-authored. And the `****** UNVERIFIED:` escape becomes permanent because nothing watches it: `boredom:274-275` authorised deferring dataset bridges; the Boredom Experiment entry was built **two days later** with five stable ids, and 37 `grounds-measure` edges plus 12 channel mappings still read *\"dataset entry not built\"*. `boredom-construct-measure-concordance.json` states `datasetEntryStatus: \"NOT BUILT … Every column→channel mapping is a flagged ****** UNVERIFIED: pointer, never a verified correspondence\"` — an entire axis of the plan's designated payoff artifact, permanently placeholder, and the concordance gate at `TEMPLATE:221` **passes it**, because the gate's own escape clause is `(or ****** UNVERIFIED:)`.\n\n---\n\n#### D16 — HIGH · The declared anchor artifact is gated on coverage, never on evidence\n`vr-ped:129-130` (schema stated in prose: `{construct, condition, sources:[{id, locus, note}]}`, \"with page anchor + one-line note incl. direction of effect\") vs `:218-219` (gate checks only that every row maps and every unit appears) · same pair at `TEMPLATE:176-177` / `:221-222` and `boredom:159-160` / `:260`\n\n**Defect:** coverage is trivially satisfiable by a mechanical join, which is what the executor built and *documented* in the artifact (\"co-occurrence of a `treats-construct` and a `tests-condition` edge in the same unit\").\n**Measured (corrected, both tolerances):** 348 cell-unit assertions; **40 backed / 308 unbacked (88.5%)** strict, **52 / 296 (85.1%)** generous; cells with ≥1 backed unit: 26 or 34 of 94. The join manufactures false claims — the cell *Presence × Home-vs-classroom* lists `ped-sec-07`, whose only authored home-vs-classroom edge is about retention and transfer; the source reports nothing about presence under that contrast.\n**And the schema was silently dropped:** 0 of 94 VR cells and 0 of 91 Boredom cells carry the mandated `locus` or `note`. The plan *did* write the schema; the gate could not see its violation, and the deviation is not recorded in `planCorrections`.\n\n---\n\n#### D17 — MEDIUM/HIGH · Registration is a hand-edit to a Python dict, performed last\n`TEMPLATE:187-197, :200-201` (\"do LAST, then GATE\")\n\n**Consequence:** **8 of 27 entries** are absent from `TEXT_DIRS` — Phantasia Secondary, RDR2 Secondary, Emotion Secondary, Motion & Time Secondary, Game-Behavior Method, RDR2 Playthrough, **Dissertation**, **Veri(dis)similitude** — including the two richest claim assets in the repo. RDR2's own gates report states the reason: registering would require hand-authoring a node-format §3A, *\"a semantic stretch\"*, so the cluster is *\"consumed directly by agents (read as files)\"* — a consumption model no code implements.\n\n---\n\n#### D18 — MEDIUM · Two hand-authored twins, one of which nothing reads\n`TEMPLATE:114, :176-177`\n\n`cluster-ontology.{md,json}` and the concordance `{md,json}` are both mandated; the compiler reads only the `.md`, and nothing requires the twins to agree. In-Game and Uncomfortable each authored 18 canonical POSITIONS into `book-level-ontology.json` — all 36 reach nothing.\n\n---\n\n#### D19 — MEDIUM · The manifest is declared authoritative and never re-derived\n`TEMPLATE:78-79, :218` · `boredom:190, :258`\n\nBoredom's `manifest.json` declares 55 units; 45 sit in top-level folders and 11 nested under `Hadjioannou (ed)/Ch01..Ch12`, so `*/*-edges.csv` finds 45 of 56. `phase0-overview.md` still reads *\"Final unit count: 46\"*, *\"revised: 46 → 45 units\"*, never mentions the 11-chapter expansion, and still ends *\"Pausing here for go-ahead.\"* `units/bor-sec-00-corpus-overview.md`, required at `:105` and `:138`, was never created — `units/` is an empty directory, in both Boredom and VR Pedagogy. **Count-mismatch is the single largest defect class: 66 of 551.**\n\n---\n\n#### D20 — MEDIUM · Gate thresholds hard-coded as literals at plan-authoring time\n`vr-ped:213` (\"Quality gates (N = 23)\"), `:216` (\"≥ 276 … 12·N\"), `:209` (23+23 agents), `:226` (\"do not re-open\")\n\nN drifted to 34 (an entire unplanned Strand F, 10 units, added mid-session by prose exchange, explicitly *\"not a formal G0 re-vote\"*). The correct floor became 408; the checkbox still reads 276. The gate passed only because 1,129 exceeded both by accident.\n\n---\n\n#### D21 — MEDIUM · No encoding, ligature or orthography policy\n\"encoding\", \"ligature\", \"diacritic\" appear nowhere in any plan. `ig-10-deep.json:425-430` documents the pypdfium2 fi/ff/fl drop it had to repair by hand (`difﬁ culty`, `sufﬁ cient`, `ﬁ gurative`). Uexküll ships four incompatible German orthographies and **the corrupted one reaches runtime** (`uex-analysis/book-level-ontology.md:27` `\"Wohnhulle\"`). The loader compounds it with a silent latin-1 fallback on UTF-8 failure. 13 encoding-corruption defects.\n\n---\n\n#### D22 — MEDIUM · Bibliographic identity frozen from a 3-page metadata skim into folder names, slugs and ids\n`vr-ped:90` + `:105-110` + `TEMPLATE:78-79`\n\n`ped-sec-14` was assigned author \"Colin\"; Colin is Robin Colin Alexander **Barrett**'s middle name. The executor caught it at Phase 1 and **declined to fix it**, recording that it kept the id/slug/folder \"as Phase 0 assigned them to match the plan's own §1C table so cross-references stay stable.\" The folder is still `Colin et al. - VR Desktop-3D and 2D (2022)/`, the files still `ped-sec-14-colin-*`, while all 30 provenance tags inside read `FAITHFUL-Barrett et al.` The same freeze left three citation-year errors and one mis-linkage documented in `_synthesis/citation-corrections-2026-07-16.md` and **still unapplied**.\n\n---\n\n#### D23 — MEDIUM · Object types and axis relations are invented per cluster with no registry\n`TEMPLATE:90-98` (\"adapt names to the domain, keep ≤12\"; \"e.g. `treats-<row-type>`\")\n\n645 distinct relation values across 219 CSVs with 41 distinct headers and 19,770 rows. No union of edges across entries is possible — which defeats the \"every point of connection\" half of the goal.\n\n---\n\n#### D24 — MEDIUM · A rendering cap promoted into a data-model cap\n`TEMPLATE:182-185` / `vr-ped:192, :222` — `≤25 edges` on the cross-pipeline `.mmd`\n\nVR Pedagogy's graph header states outright that it was aggregated to **strand** level \"to stay within the 25-edge Phase-4 cap\", shipping 8 edges over 6 nodes. The 117 unit-level bridge edges survive only as integer labels. The cap achieved its number by deleting the information.\n\n---\n\n#### D25 — MEDIUM · A minimum floor on the project's own speculation, with no ceiling\n`vr-ped:184, :220` — every unit must carry ≥1 `bridges-to-vle`/`bridges-to-part-iii` edge, all defined as `anticipatory-application` (our speculation, never the source's claim)\n\n117 speculative edges = 10.4% of the store; plus 24 `grounds-measure` edges authored to a **never-built** anchor (`vr-ped:20, :132` explicitly authorised this) and later retired wholesale.\n\n---\n\n#### D26 — LOW/MEDIUM · Unverified factual premises about source files\n`boredom:92` asserts a named PDF *is* \"the single extracted paper\" — `pdfinfo` shows 727 pages, md5-identical to a full proceedings volume. `boredom:44-85` names a paper that does not exist (Standish 2015; real paper Mansikka 2008, PDF a mislabeled Mertel duplicate), reverses an author order, and **omits two on-disk files that were the sole in-cluster grounding for the plan's own debate axis and construct row.** `boredom:41` says \"Six strands.\" and lists seven.\n\n---\n\n### 2B. REFUTED\n\n| # | Filed claim | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| **R1** | `TEMPLATE:227` \"compiler runs clean\" caused the Phantasia/RDR2/Emotion prose-dialect ontologies | **REFUTED — chronology inverted.** Template mtime 2026-07-15; those ontologies 2026-05-11, 2026-06-04, 2026-06-23. Their governing plans (`phantasia-cluster-2025-analysis.md:178`, `rdr2-secondary-cluster-analysis.md:73`) specify *no format at all*; `TEMPLATE:169-172` is the **fix**. All three clusters are also unregistered, so no gate ever evaluated on them. The compiler facts (no exit code, silent `[]`) are true, but are compiler defects, not this plan's causal output. |\n| **R2** | `vr-ped:186-187` false assumption → narrative `#### N.` headings leaked into the ontology | **REFUTED — consequence does not exist.** Re-ran the compiler's split regex on the product: 60 matches, **0** before `## 3A.` The narrative dialect (`## N.`, `**N.M ...**`) is structurally immune to both regex branches. Survives only as a LOW latent-hazard note. |\n| **R3** | `boredom-experiment-channel-schema-anchor-plan:96` (\"value is the node\") caused the 7-node entry | **REFUTED — wrong sentence.** The binding constraints are the explicit O-9/O-10 hard gates at `:104-115`. The plan *does* inventory record yield (`§2.2 :128-135`: per-channel N, 7 items, 24 episodes) and defers it deliberately to a named successor plan (`plans/boredom-experiment-o9-processing-scope-2026-07-16.md`, which specifies the 24-row schemas). Also: \"0 unit records\" is false — `units/bex-00..04` exist. The proposed fix (commit the 168-cell matrix) would **breach the consent gate**. |\n| **R4** | `plans/x.md:1` | **REFUTED — file does not exist** anywhere in the repo; defect and observation fields are single placeholder characters. |\n| **R5** | `archon-corpus-index-migration-spec.md:89-96, :138` (parity gate) caused the claim crowding-out regression | **REFUTED on four grounds.** Spec dated 2026-06-24; the measured regression is 2026-04-21 and the caps it \"mandates\" were authored 2026-04-07/09 — it transcribes, not imposes. Phases P0–P7 produced **zero** artifacts (no `corpus_*` relation exists on disk). Wrong mechanism: crowding-out is in the claim/author path (`maxClaims: 6`, already additive), not `loadCorpusIndexContext` (which has **0** references to claims). Three of the four proposed fixes shipped 31 minutes after the diagnostic. |\n| **R6** | `archon-corpus-index-migration-spec.md:58` deprioritised the claim-bearing entries | **REFUTED — non-correlated.** `Dissertation`/`Veri(dis)` never appear in any revision of `compile-corpus-index.py`, including 2026-04-07, 2.5 months before the spec. Two entries in the same \"defer\" row (Uncomfortable, Heidegger & Rhetoric) *are* registered and contribute 36 nodes each; four entries in its first-class row contribute zero. |\n| **R7** | `corpus-index-usage-plan.md` caused the empty-target cross-pipeline hooks | **REFUTED — chronology, both directions.** Plan written 2026-03-09 20:20; every hooks file authored 16:00–16:06 the same day; the compiler that materialises the defect first committed 2026-04-07. |\n\n**Pattern in the refutations:** five of seven are chronology errors or never-executed specs. Any future audit must date-stamp plan and product before asserting a chain — and the new plan should record `governing_plan` + `plan_sha` inside each entry so this is mechanical.\n\n---\n\n## 3. The gate system, judged\n\n### 3.1 Gate-by-gate\n\nLegend: **Code?** = enforced by an executable with an exit code · **Meas.?** = expressible as a number without human judgement · **Right?** = measures a property the goal cares about.\n\n| # | Gate (line) | Threshold | Code? | Meas.? | Right? | At N=1 | At claim level |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| G-1 | N units × 3 files on disk (`TEMPLATE:218`) | presence | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | trivially true | meaningless — 3 files can hold 5 or 500 records |\n| G-2 | ≥12·N dedup global edges (`:219`) | 12N | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | =12, trivial | 1–2 orders low; **anti-correlated** — destructive dedup makes it easier |\n| G-3 | 8–12 documented debates (`:219`) | band | ✗ | ✗ | partly | **0 by construction** — verified: 12/12 Phantasia and 11/11 Boredom axes are multi-unit | fixed band caps recorded disagreement |\n| G-4 | 8–12 contested readings (`:219`) | band | ✗ | ✗ | ✓ | **survives** if re-based on external interlocutors (VR CR-01/CR-03 contest Short et al. 1976 and the SSQ, neither a cluster unit) | should be a per-claim `contested_by[]`, not a count |\n| G-5 | ≥50 terminology lemmas (`:220`) | 50 | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | arbitrary | orthogonal; 20× spread across entries (Phantasia 213/8 units vs Boredom 72/55) all passing |\n| G-6 | ≥max(10, N/4) intra-cluster citations (`:220`) | 10 | ✗ | ✗ | ✓ | **unsatisfiable by construction** | cross-source only |\n| G-7 | Concordance coverage + `(or ****** UNVERIFIED:)` (`:221-222`) | 100% | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | degenerate | **self-defeating** — the escape clause passes an entirely unmapped axis (Boredom: \"SATISFIED 12/12\", all twelve placeholders) |\n| G-8 | Every anchor-strand unit ≥1 bridge edge (`:223-224`) | ≥1 | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | **survives — best-formed gate in §8** | right shape, wrong granularity; checks presence, never resolution (`grounds-measure` 0/37) |\n| G-9 | No ≥25-word verbatim (`:225`) | 25w | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ | unchanged | **actively hostile** — forbids the target atom; named checker does not exist |\n| G-10 | Provenance tags \"throughout\" (`:225`) | — | ✗ | ✗ | ✓ | unchanged | unmeasurable: no unit of quantification, no required field (only 67 of 463 Boredom readings carry a tag value; 201 null) |\n| G-11 | 5 Mermaid graphs render; ≤25 edges (`:226`) | 5 / 25 | ✗ | ✓* | ✗ | 2 of 5 render empty | render cap ≠ data cap; `mmdc` v11.14.0 **is** installed, RDR2 recorded \"not installed\" |\n| G-12 | Parseable `## 3A` (`:227`) | present | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | unchanged | **measures a marker the parser ignores** |\n| G-13 | Compiler runs clean (`:227`) | — | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ | always passes | always passes — `main()` cannot fail |\n| G-14 | compiled counts verified by reading (`:227-228`) | — | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | **works** | **best gate in §8** but human-run, node/term only, and with **no declared expected value** — a low-but-nonzero yield passes (Social Presence 10, Rhetoric of Interactivity 7, vs Boredom 61) |\n| G-15 | Verbatim detector clean (`:228`) | — | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ | n/a | **references a tool that does not exist** |\n| G-16 | Backups + G0 + G1, no commit before G1 (`:229`) | — | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | **survives** | **survives — the only structurally sound line in §8** |\n| G-17 | Per-unit edge floors 12/20/35 (`:162`) | 12/20/35 | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | **survives — already per-unit** | measures effort not coverage: 0 violations in 55 units while density ranged 0.19–1.67 readings/page |\n\n\\* checkable in principle; the gate names no command and requires no evidence artifact.\n\n### 3.2 Verdict on the cross-unit-gate argument\n\nThe claim that \"most gates collapse at N=1\" is **overstated, and the overstatement matters** because it would license discarding gates that are salvageable. The correct, evidence-checked position:\n\n**Genuinely GROUP-scope — evaluate to nothing at N=1, no substitute possible:**\n1. **Documented debates (G-3)** — verified multi-unit in every instance examined (12/12 Phantasia, 11/11 Boredom, minimum 3 units per axis).\n2. **Intra-cluster citation network (G-6)** — worse than collapse: the `max(10, …)` form is *unsatisfiable*, which taught executors to talk past gates (RDR2: \"a finding, not a shortfall of the build\").\n3. **Scholarly-evolution arc** (`TEMPLATE:123, :179-180`) — the date range is a point.\n\n**NOT cross-unit, contrary to the filed claim:**\n- **Contested readings (G-4)** survive intact when contestation is against a *named external interlocutor*. They are currently unmeasurable for a different reason: no record format at all (VR Pedagogy: free prose with `**CR-NN.**` run-ins, 18 declared vs 21 regex hits).\n- **The concordance (G-7)** survives. Phantasia's is keyed `loci_by_work` — *source × locus*. At N=1 it becomes the single row of locus cells one article fills, which is exactly the addressable payload the goal wants.\n- **Concept nodes** survive: 9 of 41 gold-cluster concepts are already single-unit.\n- **Edge floors (G-17)** are per-unit by construction; the cluster-level 12·N restatement is redundant.\n\n**Therefore:** move 3 gates to an additive GROUP layer with an explicit `N/A-by-construction` emission below a declared minimum membership (≥5, since the three ratified clusters sit at N=2,3,4). Keep everything else at ENTRY scope and re-express it as a per-source intensive quantity. Skipping a GROUP gate must be a recorded **pass**, not a waiver.\n\n### 3.3 Gates satisfied by agent self-attestation rather than by a check\n\n**All 17 are. Zero gates in the entire lineage are enforced by code.** Ranked by how far self-attestation travels from the truth:\n\n| Gate | How it is \"satisfied\" | Evidence it was wrong |\n|---|---|---|\n| **G-9 verbatim ban** | agent asserts | RDR2 report: *\"per-unit agents verified (longest ~19 w)\"* — self-report; ≥4 fabricated spans shipped in `ped-sec-29` |\n| **G-15 verbatim detector** | narration only | the tool does not exist |\n| **G-13 compiler clean** | process returned | 55 tension records discarded with 0 warnings |\n| **G-10 provenance throughout** | agent asserts | 201 of 463 Boredom readings have a null tag; 195 have a null stance |\n| **G-7 concordance complete** | prose strings inside the artifact it judges (`\"SATISFIED 55/55\"`, `\"columnToChannelGate: SATISFIED 12/12\"`) | all 12 are placeholders |\n| **G-11 graphs render** | asserted or deferred | RDR2 deferred on a false premise (`mmdc` is installed) |\n| **G-3/G-4/G-5/G-6 counts** | typed into prose or embedded self-attested `gate{}` objects (Boredom `citation-network.json` carries its own `{required:10, deliveredTotal:65, satisfied:true}`) | VR shipped 18 contested readings against a stated band of 8–12, unflagged |\n| **G-1 completeness** | `ls` | `units/` empty in both entries; three units with 0 readings pass |\n| **G-14 compiled counts** | human reads two integers | 19 of 60 VR nodes corrupted; count was correct, content was not |\n| **G-16 backups/G1** | asserted | Boredom's `.backups/` contains 9 files, none of them the two the plan names |\n\n**Structural fault:** gate objects are embedded *inside the artifacts they judge*, authored by the agent that produced them. There is no separation of producer and judge anywhere in the process.\n\n---\n\n## 4. What the plans never say\n\nRanked by damage done (defect count × reach). These are the gaps executing agents filled differently every time.\n\n| Rank | Unspecified | Damage |\n|---|---|---|\n| **1** | **What a CLAIM is.** No plan defines a claim record, id, granularity or yield. `readings[]` (`TEMPLATE:159`) and `positions` (Uncomfortable) are the nearest, and both are one-line array names. Only `tmp/Dissertation/DISSERTATION-ANALYSIS-PIPELINE-PLAN.md` ever wrote it down (\"a discrete proposition that could plausibly be true or false, contested or supported\", with a worked 3-claims-in-one-sentence decomposition). | The entire granularity ceiling: ~7 records/source vs a 50–500 target |\n| **2** | **What a CLAUSE is.** No plan names a sentence index, character span or bbox. The finest addresses in the corpus arrived *incidentally* — Bekker line pairs, In-Game line ranges into a deleted `/tmp` file, RDR2 VTT timestamps, VLE respondent×item keys. | Clause level absent from all 1,758 files |\n| **3** | **Element schemas for every nested array.** Key names only. | 42 shapes in one entry; 49 schema-violation defects |\n| **4** | **Which files the loader opens.** Never stated in any plan. | 8 unregistered entries; 18+18 JSON-only positions lost; ~98% of every template entry unreachable |\n| **5** | **`tension-edges.json` and its `node_a`/`node_b` contract.** | 55 records discarded silently; 4 of 11 files yield zero |\n| **6** | **Id grammar, uniqueness, namespacing, prefix registry.** | 42 colliding values across 8 units; 296 unaddressable readings; 91 id-less Wendt claims; 20 fused cross-entry nodes; 10 id-prefix + 10 id-collision defects |\n| **7** | **Controlled values for categorical fields.** Only *object types* and *edge relations* are controlled, never field values. | `stance`: 162–170 distinct values, 195 nulls, 138 hapaxes; `claim_type`: 15 uncontrolled in the sandbox, ~36 corpus-wide; `FAITHFUL-` degenerates into 85 keys incl. `FAITHFUL-B`, `FAITHFUL-DB`, `FAITHFUL-O`; `INTERP-med` vs `INTERP-medium` |\n| **8** | **The dedup key, and whether losses must be reported.** | 18 + 2 evidence-distinct rows destroyed; 19,770 rows on disk ≈ 9,762 distinct triples with no record of which layer is authoritative |\n| **9** | **Retention, hashing and versioning of the extracted text.** | ~1,000 In-Game clause pointers dead; VR Pedagogy fabrication undiagnosable from its own materials |\n| **10** | **Page-offset model, and that it can be non-constant.** | Aristotle 33/34 wrong by ≤47pp; bekker-index 101/188 off by >2; Rickert declared 20, drifts to 15 |\n| **11** | **Locator resolvability.** Loci must be \"carried\", never resolved. | 961 concordance cells say \"implicit-throughout\"; 6,961 bare numbers with no declared numbering system; 197 Boredom edges carry `n/a` or a provenance tag in the locus column |\n| **12** | **The parser's actual transformations** — that a heading parenthetical becomes `greek` and enters a corpus-wide greedy-match list; that a node missing a `type` bullet inherits its `centrality` as its type (73 runtime nodes affected). | 204 of 701 nodes poisoned; bare English words matching corpus-wide |\n| **13** | **Where a provenance tag lives** — prose or field. | VR Pedagogy: 1,136 prose tokens vs 233 fields |\n| **14** | **A rights model.** One copyright assumption hardcoded for a template meant to process \"ANY folder\". | Verbatim suppressed for public-domain Equiano/Radcliffe/Austen/Darwin and for the user's own work |\n| **15** | **A record-density target.** Prose word bands are the only volume instruction. | 1,277 prose assertions vs 233 structured readings |\n| **16** | **N=1 behaviour and scope-tagging of deliverables.** | Thin entries silently dropped the mandated artifact set rather than adapting it; no single-source entry has a gates report |\n| **17** | **That gates must emit a machine-readable result.** | 2/27 reports, 1/27 metrics |\n| **18** | **Separation of author and judge.** | Every surviving gate record is self-attestation |\n| **19** | **Reconciliation of `****** UNVERIFIED:` once the blocker clears.** | 37 edges + 12 mappings still \"not built\" 13 days after the target entry landed; 22 live \"not yet built\" assertions corpus-wide |\n| **20** | **Negative evidence as a record.** `\"Not treated:\"` is mandated in prose (`TEMPLATE:158`) and appears in **no JSON array** — bor-sec-30 lists 8 explicitly-absent measures, bor-sec-13 lists 3 absent constructs. | A machine-checkable claim class is written and discarded |\n| **21** | **Idempotency / re-run / growth contract.** Nothing says what a second execution does, how ids are reserved, or what invalidates dependent records when a source is re-extracted. | Incremental growth of the index is undefined; `Dissertation` carries two full identical run-histories with no rule for which counts |\n| **22** | **Manifest re-derivation from disk; cross-artifact numeric consistency.** | 66 count-mismatch defects |\n| **23** | **Source admissibility** (text-layer sanity, citation completeness). | `ptf-01` shipped with an identical per-page text hash and all verbatims UNVERIFIED; `riv-02` with an unverified venue |\n| **24** | **Encoding/orthography normalisation.** | Uexküll's corrupted German is the variant that reaches runtime |\n| **25** | **A downstream-citation index.** | A corrected VLE figure left 12 stale live copies in a sibling entry |\n| **26** | **Plan supersession and fact migration.** | v2's byte-verified 12-column HMD schema, 24-cell inventory and 4-channel S05 result stranded in a plan file |\n| **27** | **A query surface.** Zero references to any claim store across `src/` and `scripts/`. | An index nobody can query cannot improve drafting |\n| **28** | **A budget/cost model.** Only reference points: $1.33/paper for claim extraction, ~$0.30/drafting run. | Scope set by guesswork |\n\n---\n\n## 5. What must be preserved\n\nThese are not incidental. Several are the only reason this audit was possible.\n\n**P1 — GATE G0 (`TEMPLATE:100-103`).** A cheap, early, human sign-off on scope, axes and vocabulary *before* any expensive authoring. Correcting the vocabulary at spec time costs one turn; correcting it after 55 agents costs the build. **Extend what G0 approves to include the record schema and the density band.**\n\n**P2 — GATE G1 + no-commit-before-G1 + timestamped `.backups/` (`TEMPLATE:189, :200-201, :229`).** The only structurally sound line in §8. **Change *what* G1 is shown** — a machine-readable gates report, not a dict diff and two integers — and **move registration off the end** so an entry is visible-and-empty on day one.\n\n**P3 — `manifest.json → planCorrections` (`TEMPLATE:214`, `boredom:214`).** Genuinely excellent and demonstrably used. Boredom's seven corrections each carry issue / files / **evidence array with the verification command and its output** / resolution / residual. Correction #7 caught the plan **contradicting itself** (`:208` Strand-A vs `:261` Strand-A/B), resolved to the more specific rule, **refused to fabricate three edges**, cited per-source evidence for each refusal, and deliberately declined to edit the plan so the contradiction stayed visible. Nothing else in 27 entries comes close. **Formalise the schema; pair it with gates — it catches what agents notice, gates catch what they do not** (it missed `bor-sec-00` entirely).\n\n**P4 — The no-fabrication norm with an escalation path.** The `bor-sec-18` agent refused to build a unit under a false attribution when its PDF proved to be a mislabeled duplicate, and escalated. **\"Refuse and escalate\" must remain an explicitly sanctioned agent outcome.**\n\n**P5 — The three-tag provenance discipline (`TEMPLATE:38-42`).** `FE` / `FAITHFUL-<AUTHOR>` / `P·anticipatory-application`. The most consistently applied idea in the corpus (2,761 / 1,323 / 1,196 / 524 occurrences) and the mechanism that keeps the user's readings separable from the sources'. **Keep the concept; close the vocabulary; move it from prose into a required field.**\n\n**P6 — The anchor discipline: bridge, never re-digest (`TEMPLATE:30-36`).** Cite the anchor's own unit ids; find its canonical id list before authoring. This is what stops N single-source entries becoming N re-explanations of the same book. **Strengthen into a resolved-reference requirement.**\n\n**P7 — Enumerating cross-entry target ids literally in the plan (`boredom:24`).** 100% resolution where done, 0% where not. **Do it for every relation, or ship the command that generates the list.**\n\n**P8 — Declaring closed axis vocabularies verbatim in the plan (`boredom:147-157`).** 96% conformance across 55 independent agents, and the reason Boredom has none of the double-registry defect that hit Uncomfortable. **Declare inline, never by reference.**\n\n**P9 — The de-dup / haystack rubric (`TEMPLATE:57-67`).** md5 DROP, same-study MERGE with `dup-variant`, `>300pp` HAYSTACK with grep-locate and `-f/-l` re-extraction, `HAYSTACK-UNRESOLVED` flag, dispositions persisted to `manifest.excluded` with md5 evidence. Concrete, mechanical, executed, and it produced two real salvages.\n\n**P10 — Mandatory pre-extraction with agents given the `.txt` path, never the PDF (`TEMPLATE:137-140`).** Correct for cost and for the known multi-page-image API-400 failure. **Change only the destination:** committed and hashed, not scratch.\n\n**P11 — The OCR-LOW check.** `pdftotext` word-count sanity with a documented fallback; correctly caught two 0-word sources and recorded the audit range in the manifest.\n\n**P12 — The reliability lesson (`TEMPLATE:208-210`).** The documented ~1-in-8 subagent no-op with a mandatory post-batch sweep — the one enforced check in the plan, 100% trio completeness on all three template-lineage clusters. **Keep the sweep; upgrade what it checks from existence to conformance; delete \"self-author any gaps\".**\n\n**P13 — The agent context bundle (`TEMPLATE:211-213`) and a named quality exemplar.** Right mechanism; the exemplar must itself be a schema-valid, reachable record set.\n\n**P14 — `\"Not treated:\"` (`TEMPLATE:158`).** Negative evidence, rare and directly serving \"every weakness\". **Promote from a trailing prose line to a first-class record type.**\n\n**P15 — The Wendt double-locus rule** (`plans/wendt-design-for-dasein-analysis.md:129`, `(p.NN / pdf NN)` on every citation). Measured **307/307 = 100%**. Precisely specified + regex-checkable + per-record is the exact recipe that works. **Generalise to a triple locus (printed / pdf / char-span).**\n\n**P16 — The `Uncomfortable Situations` offset artifact.** `us-literary-loci-concordance.json` declares `page_offset_rule`, `tier_rule`, and per-locus records carrying `specific_anchor`, `appears_in_units`, `first_cited_pdf_page`, `tier`, `role`. **Make it mandatory per source.**\n\n**P17 — The artifacts the template abstracted away and must be restored:** Phantasia's `render-validation.txt` (tool version, exact invocation, per-graph PASS table) and RDR2's `quality-gates-report.md` with its explicit **\"Gates NOT fully met (reported honestly)\"** section. Both were produced unbidden; both stopped once the template replaced hand-written plans. **Make honest under-report a required section, not a happy accident.**\n\n**P18 — The Dissertation pipeline's contract-manifest pattern:** `claim_count_target: \"140-180\"` / `claim_count_actual: 156` / `schema_version` / `support_tier_distribution` stamped into the artifact. The only pre-declared expectation anywhere in the corpus.\n\n**P19 — Veri(dis)similitude's `disposition` and `[V:…]` volatility flags.** 157/157 populated. The only fields in the corpus that make the index *actionable during drafting* and that turn a vocabulary change into a work queue rather than silent rot.\n\n**P20 — Immutable `_run-history/<ts>/` + `_living/latest.md`.** Good reproducibility shape; add a single-run-of-record rule.\n\n**P21 — Depth tiering with two-pass on long works, and chapter-selective decomposition.** Boredom correctly turned an edited volume into 11 addressable chapter units.\n\n**P22 — `****** UNVERIFIED:` + do-not-stall (`TEMPLATE:8-10`).** Keep the doctrine. **Give the marker a field to live in and a reconciliation trigger.**\n\n---\n\n## 6. The claim and clause schema — proposed\n\n### 6.0 Design axiom\n\n**Separate the ADDRESS from the TEXT.** Every claim carries a machine-verifiable address into a committed, hashed text projection, *whether or not* the verbatim is stored or displayable. Rights govern **display**, never **storage or verification**. This resolves the copyright/clause-level contradiction that has shaped the entire corpus away from span-level indexing.\n\n### 6.1 The CLAUSE record\n\nThe addressable span of source text, independently identified, **referenced by** claims rather than nested inside them (one clause grounds many claims; one claim spans several clauses).\n\n| Field | Type | Justified by |\n|---|---|---|\n| `clause_id` | `<DOC>-CL<nnnnn>` | net-new; required for many-to-many |\n| `doc_id` | sha256(source file) + `edition_key` | In-Game addressed `/tmp`; Aristotle addressed \"the PDF\" and a superseded offset silently poisoned 33/34 unit records |\n| `text_layer_id` | → `{tool, tool_version, exact_command, flags, text_sha256, extracted_at}` | two extractions give different offsets; without this every offset is a guess |\n| `char_start` / `char_end` | int into that text layer | **NET-NEW — the single structural addition that moves the corpus from page to clause** |\n| `sentence_index` | int | net-new |\n| `line_start` / `line_end` | int | already in use and cheaply recoverable: In-Game 858 line refs; Dissertation anchors 982/982 by line |\n| `page_pdf` / `page_printed` | int | universal; `page_printed` derived through the offset map |\n| `citation_address` | typed union (below) | Aristotle `aristotle-bekker-index.json` `{bekker, description, concepts[], pdf_page, unit_id, work}` — an edition-independent address stored *alongside* a rendering-specific one |\n| `quote` | exact text | Dissertation's 235 cached verbatims prove claim+words-linked works |\n| `quote_sha256`, `quote_word_count` | | the hash is the address that survives re-extraction; the word count drives the rights gate |\n| `normalized_quote` | NFC, ligature-repaired, whitespace-collapsed | Uexkull/Uexküll/Uexkuell in one entry; pdfium drops fi/ff/fl invisibly |\n| `rights_tier` | enum: `own-work \\| public-domain \\| licensed \\| third-party-copyright` | one hardcoded assumption at `TEMPLATE:44` suppressed verbatim across public-domain and own-work sources alike |\n| `redact_on_render` | bool | derived from `rights_tier` + `quote_word_count`; governs display only |\n| `insertion_anchor` | short verbatim phrase of the *target* text | Dissertation: 235/235; the corpus's only content-addressed pointer that **still resolves today**, unlike line ranges |\n\n**`citation_address` variants, each already in use somewhere:**\n- `bekker {work, book, chapter, bekker_start, bekker_end}` — Aristotle: 2,323 loci with line numbers, **already a clause-level address system**\n- `heidegger_h {h_page}` — BT prose (\"H.96\", \"H.95–101\")\n- `section {section_ref}` — \"§21\", \"§9b-β\"\n- `timestamp {ms_start, ms_end, frame_id}` — RDR2 Playthrough: 1,040 frame ids + 529 timestamps, **below clause level on the temporal axis**\n- `dataset_cell {subject, condition, item}` — Boredom Experiment / VLE\n- `page_range {page_start, page_end}` — the universal fallback\n\n**Graceful degradation ladder** (record `locator_precision` explicitly, and gate on the distribution):\n\n| Precision | Requirement | Reason code when degraded |\n|---|---|---|\n| `char-span` | source has an extractable text layer | — |\n| `line-range` | text layer exists, offsets not computed | `OFFSETS-DEFERRED` |\n| `bekker` / `h-page` / `section` | canonical numbering present in source | — (equivalent to clause level; **not** a degradation) |\n| `timestamp` | AV source | — |\n| `page` | OCR-degraded or image-only source | `OCR-LOW`, `NO-TEXT-LAYER` |\n| `none` | forbidden | build fails |\n\n### 6.2 The CLAIM record\n\n| Field | Type | Justified by |\n|---|---|---|\n| `claim_id` | `<ENTRY>-<UNIT>-C<nnnn>`, globally unique, registered | Dissertation declares `claim_id_format` and achieves 982 with zero collisions; BT 108/108 distinct; BCAP 146; VDS 157. Counter-proof: Wendt 91 id-less, 20 colliding; Boredom 42 values colliding across 8 units |\n| `entry_id`, `unit_id` | required | Wendt's per-file `C1` is meaningless without them |\n| `claim_text` | ≤60 words, **our paraphrase** | canonical name from Dissertation (422 records); the same field is spelled `tx`, `text`, `claim`, `statement` across 6 entries — pick one |\n| `claim_kind` | **closed enum** (§6.3) | Dissertation `claim_type` populated 982/982 → the facet is wanted; it has **378 distinct values** → it must be closed |\n| `scope` | **closed enum** | Being and Time `status` — the only place argumentative altitude is recorded, and 101/108 rows controlled |\n| `stance` | **closed enum** | Boredom 162–170 free values / 195 nulls / 138 hapaxes. **Critical bug to design out:** `stance: \"FE\"` occurs 22 times — a provenance tag in the stance field. Disjoint enums, both required, validator rejects cross-contamination |\n| `support_tier` | **closed 8-value enum** | Dissertation `support_tier_legend`, exercised on 982 records. **This is the field that delivers \"every weakness\"** |\n| `evidence_type` | **closed enum** | Von Uexküll's `Evidence type` column, 107/107 — the only place in the corpus separating *what kind* of evidence from *how strong* |\n| `strength_rationale` | free text, **separate field** | Uexküll glued rationale to enum with an em-dash → ~100 values from a 3-value vocabulary; BCAP glued page numbers in. **Never fuse an enum and its prose** |\n| `provenance` | **closed enum** + registry-resolved author slot | `TEMPLATE:38-42`, the most-used idea in the corpus; needs a registry because free surnames produced `FAITHFUL-B`, `FAITHFUL-DB`, `FAITHFUL-O`, and doubled forms |\n| `clause_refs[]` | array of `clause_id`, min 1 | the join that makes the index clause-addressable |\n| `locator_precision` | enum | makes degradation visible and gateable |\n| `premises[]` | **ordered array** of `{index, text, ref}` | BCAP's enumerated premises + explicit `→ conclusion` step (150 records); BT `premises` 108/108. **Both encode them as ONE PROSE CELL** — which is why nothing can traverse them |\n| `supports[]` / `supported_by[]` | `claim_id[]` | Dissertation: 76% of 982 in an explicit support graph, 841 typed edges. **This is \"every point of connection\"** |\n| `contests[]` / `contested_by[]` | `claim_id[]` or `interlocutor_id[]` | Uncomfortable positions carry `contested_by`; BT carries 84 explicit claim→tension back-refs |\n| `tension_ids[]` | `tension_id[]` | BT's 84 back-refs + `contested-nodes.md`. **The second half of \"every weakness\"** |\n| `cites_primary[]` / `cites_secondary[]` / `implicit_citations_needed[]` | `{locus, tier, rationale}[]` | Dissertation `pCit/sCit/iCit` 982/982. **The third slot is what makes the index an instrument** — it names the citation the prose is *missing* |\n| `interlocutors[]` | `{interlocutor_id, role (enum), locus}` | Uncomfortable's 176 loci records carry `role`; VDS carries `role` + `corpus_index_bridge` |\n| `analytic_anchor[]` | project-closed enum | VDS's declared RODA enum (12 values, ~240 attachments over 157 rows); RDR2 beat-maps' \"RODA locus\" column. The corpus-wide generalisation of the concordance idea |\n| `surface_form` | the source's own wording | `TEMPLATE:81-88` normalises the source's term away into a free-text note; the goal needs both |\n| `coined_terms[]` | string[] | Dissertation `coined_terms_present` + canonical-definition-sites index — polices the project's own vocabulary |\n| `flag_present` : bool + `flag_text` : the quoted hedge | | Dissertation: pairing the boolean with the actual hedge is what makes `T3-interpretive-but-flagged` **auditable rather than asserted** |\n| `disposition` | **closed 5-value enum** | VDS 157/157 (`re-ground` 127, `enrich` 21, `keep` 7, `supersede` 2). The only forward-looking field in the corpus |\n| `volatility` | `{is_volatile, depends_on, resolved_at, note}` | VDS `[V:…]` flags with in-place resolution stamps |\n| `remediation` | `{action (enum), corpus_index_candidates[], chroma_candidates[], external_query, effort}` | Dissertation `rem` 982/982, with real routing values |\n| `use_scope` | enum `index-only \\| citable-pending-<gate> \\| citable` | Boredom Experiment's O-10 was applied as an **entry-wide content ceiling**, permanently capping granularity; a per-record field indexes the 168-cell matrix now while blocking quotation |\n| `derivation` | enum `agent-read \\| self-authored \\| inferred \\| script-derived` | `TEMPLATE:210` authorises self-authoring with no marker |\n| `confidence` + `needs_human_review` | enum + bool | BCAP already emits 30 `**Confidence**` bullets with no field to live in |\n| `extraction` | `{tool, tool_version, exact_command, source_sha256, text_layer_id, text_sha256, run_id, extracted_at}` | In-Game's 858 line refs died because nothing recorded how to regenerate the text |\n| `schema_version` | string | only Dissertation stamps one; nothing else can be migrated safely |\n\n### 6.3 Controlled vocabularies — union-and-dedup from actual use\n\n**`support_tier` (8, adopted verbatim from Dissertation; observed over 982 records):**\n`T1-textually-confirmed` 277 · `T2-textually-supported` 78 · `T3-interpretive-but-flagged` 477 · `T4-interpretive-but-unflagged` 41 · `T5-under-supported` 71 · `T6-unsupported` 12 · `T7-overreach` 22 · `T8-secondary-needed` 4.\n*Migration crosswalk:* Uexküll `Strong`→T1/T2, `Moderate`→T3/T5, `Weak`→T6; BCAP `Explicitly stated`/`Textually explicit`→T1, `[INTERP-high]`→T3; VDS tier 1→T1, tier 2→T3.\n\n**`provenance` (complete observed vocabulary, with corpus-wide counts):**\n`FE` 2,761 · `P/anticipatory-application` 1,323 · `burke-direct` 1,196 · `anticipatory-application` 524 *(merge into `P/…`)* · `INTERP-high` 380 · `INTERP-low` 368 · `calleja-direct` 180 · `INTERP-med` 29 + `INTERP-medium` 21 *(merge)* · `FE-U` · `FE-STUDENT` · `FE-TEACHER` · `FAITHFUL:<author_key>` across **85 distinct keys** (top: Slaby 175, Makransky 154, Parong 144, Richardson 132, Keane 130, Yakobi 108, Nacke 102, Tam 102, Seo 98, Kim 94, Holmqvist 88, Mansikka 86). Bracketed forms (`[INTERP-high]` 276, `[INTERP-low]` 207, `[FE]` 43, `[P]` 33, `[FE-STUDENT]` 12, `[FE-U]` 10) normalise to bare. **`FAITHFUL` author keys must resolve against a per-entry interlocutor registry** — the free-surname convention already produced `FAITHFUL-B`, `FAITHFUL-C`, `FAITHFUL-DB`, `FAITHFUL-De`, `FAITHFUL-Tu`, and doubled forms (`FAITHFUL-Slaby` 175 vs `FAITHFUL-Slaby & Thonhauser` 8).\n\n**`stance` (union-and-dedup of Boredom's 170 + VR Pedagogy's 66 free values):**\n`asserts · defines · classifies · reports · extends · refines · qualifies · concedes · contests · refutes · restates · synthesizes · concludes · self-critiques · defers`. Null illegal. All nuance goes to a separate `note`.\n\n**`claim_kind`:** `assertion · definition · textual-report · interpretation · premise · conclusion · methodological · programmatic · quotation · contrast · open-question · **negative-claim**` (the last from `\"Not treated:\"`, currently discarded).\n\n**`scope`** (from BT `status`, splitting kind from altitude): `book-thesis` 42 · `chapter-thesis` 11 · `section-thesis` 4 · `unit-thesis` · `local-support` 36 · `transitional`.\n\n**`evidence_type`** (12, collapsing Uexküll's 105 glued values): `textual-explicit · textual-inferred · philosophical-argument · empirical-experiment · empirical-observation · comparative · analogical · diagrammatic · statistical · anecdotal · authority-citation · methodological-principle`.\n\n**`disposition`** (VDS, 5): `keep-verbatim · re-ground · enrich · supersede · drop`.\n\n**Extension rule:** any value not in an enum must be filed in a per-entry `vocabulary-extensions.json` with a one-line justification and a declared parent, **written back to the global registry in the same commit** — never inlined.\n\n### 6.4 Worked example\n\n**Source record** (real, from `corpus/index/Dissertation/_run-history/2026-05-20T0058/_per-section/DISS-03-A3/phase2-claims.json`):\n\n```json\n{ \"claim_id\": \"DISS-03-C001\", \"section_id\": \"DISS-03-A3\", \"subsection_id\": \"DISS-03-S1\",\n  \"location\": { \"line_start\": 5, \"line_end\": 5 },\n  \"claim_text\": \"The actualization of perception terminates not in an ephemeral event but in a residual composite consisting of dual-traces — a resonant kinēsis constituted by resonant aisthēma (formal-epistemic content) and resonant orexis (affective valence) — that persists after the sensible object has withdrawn.\",\n  \"claim_type\": \"interpretive-architectural\", \"logical_role\": \"transition-from-§1.2\",\n  \"supports\": [\"DISS-03-C002\",\"DISS-03-C003\"], \"supported_by\": [\"DISS-02-section-conclusion-from-§1.2\"],\n  \"implicit_citations_needed\": [{ \"locus\": \"DA II.5, 417a-b; On Dreams 459a24-460b3 (residual motion mechanics)\",\n      \"status\": \"T2-textually-supported\", \"rationale\": \"User asserts this as established at §1.2; verify the §1.2 grounding is locked.\" }],\n  \"support_tier\": \"T2-textually-supported\", \"is_coined_term_present\": true,\n  \"coined_terms_present\": [\"resonant kinēsis\",\"resonant aisthēma\",\"resonant orexis\"],\n  \"interpretive_flag_present\": true, \"interpretive_flag_text\": \"'as I established in the preceding section'\",\n  \"remediation\": {\"action\":\"NONE\",\"estimated_remediation_effort\":\"none — established at §1.2\"} }\n```\n\n**Same claim in the proposed schema** — note that everything added is either a locator, an enum-closure, or a provenance field; nothing is invented:\n\n```jsonc\n{ \"schema_version\": \"IDX-CLAIM-v1\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"DISS-03-C0001\", \"entry_id\": \"DISS\", \"unit_id\": \"DISS-03-A3\", \"section_id\": \"DISS-03-S1\",\n\n  \"claim_text\": \"The actualization of perception terminates not in an ephemeral event but in a residual composite of dual-traces — resonant kinēsis, constituted by resonant aisthēma and resonant orexis — persisting after the sensible object has withdrawn.\",\n  \"claim_kind\": \"interpretation\", \"scope\": \"section-thesis\", \"stance\": \"asserts\",\n  \"logical_role\": \"transition-from-§1.2\",\n\n  \"clause_refs\": [\"DISS-03-CL00012\"], \"locator_precision\": \"char-span\",\n\n  \"support_tier\": \"T2-textually-supported\", \"evidence_type\": \"textual-inferred\",\n  \"strength_rationale\": \"Rests on §1.2's residual-motion grounding, not on a locus in this section.\",\n  \"provenance\": \"FE\",                                   // own-work: the user's own prose\n  \"flag_present\": true, \"flag_text\": \"'as I established in the preceding section'\",\n\n  \"premises\": [ {\"index\":1,\"text\":\"Perception actualizes as kinēsis.\",\"ref\":\"DISS-02-C0087\"},\n                {\"index\":2,\"text\":\"Residual motion persists post-withdrawal.\",\"ref\":\"ARIST-DA-CL00431\"} ],\n  \"supports\": [\"DISS-03-C0002\",\"DISS-03-C0003\"], \"supported_by\": [\"DISS-02-C0114\"],\n  \"contests\": [], \"contested_by\": [], \"tension_ids\": [],\n\n  \"cites_primary\": [], \"cites_secondary\": [],\n  \"implicit_citations_needed\": [ { \"locus\": {\"type\":\"bekker\",\"work\":\"De Anima\",\"book\":\"II\",\"chapter\":\"5\",\"bekker_start\":\"417a\",\"bekker_end\":\"417b\"},\n      \"tier\":\"T2-textually-supported\", \"rationale\":\"Residual-motion mechanics; verify the §1.2 grounding is locked.\" },\n    { \"locus\": {\"type\":\"bekker\",\"work\":\"On Dreams\",\"bekker_start\":\"459a24\",\"bekker_end\":\"460b3\"},\n      \"tier\":\"T2-textually-supported\", \"rationale\":\"Same.\" } ],\n\n  \"interlocutors\": [ {\"interlocutor_id\":\"ARIST\",\"role\":\"anchor\",\n      \"locus\":{\"type\":\"bekker\",\"work\":\"De Anima\",\"book\":\"II\",\"chapter\":\"5\",\"bekker_start\":\"417a\"}} ],\n  \"analytic_anchor\": [\"A1-perception\",\"A2-phantasma\"],\n  \"surface_form\": \"resonant kinēsis\",\n  \"coined_terms\": [\"resonant kinēsis\",\"resonant aisthēma\",\"resonant orexis\"],\n\n  \"disposition\": \"keep-verbatim\",\n  \"volatility\": {\"is_volatile\": false},\n  \"remediation\": {\"action\":\"NONE\",\"corpus_index_candidates\":[\"DISS:DISS-02-S3\"],\"effort\":\"none\"},\n\n  \"use_scope\": \"citable\", \"derivation\": \"agent-read\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\", \"needs_human_review\": false,\n  \"extraction\": { \"tool\":\"pdftotext\",\"tool_version\":\"24.02.0\",\"exact_command\":\"pdftotext -layout DISS-03-A3.pdf -\",\n      \"source_sha256\":\"…\",\"text_layer_id\":\"DISS-03-A3@1\",\"text_sha256\":\"…\",\"run_id\":\"2026-05-20T0058\",\"extracted_at\":\"2026-05-20T00:58:14Z\" } }\n```\n\n**And its clause** — the record type that does not exist anywhere today:\n\n```jsonc\n{ \"clause_id\": \"DISS-03-CL00012\", \"doc_id\": \"sha256:…\", \"edition_key\": \"DISS-03-A3-v4\",\n  \"text_layer_id\": \"DISS-03-A3@1\",\n  \"char_start\": 1184, \"char_end\": 1462, \"sentence_index\": 7, \"line_start\": 5, \"line_end\": 5,\n  \"page_pdf\": 3, \"page_printed\": 3,\n  \"citation_address\": { \"type\": \"section\", \"section_ref\": \"§1.3\" },\n  \"quote\": \"…the actualization terminates in a residual composite…\",\n  \"quote_sha256\": \"…\", \"quote_word_count\": 41,\n  \"normalized_quote\": \"…\", \n  \"rights_tier\": \"own-work\", \"redact_on_render\": false,\n  \"insertion_anchor\": \"they are a *movement* (kinēsis) of the soul, a dynamic reorientation\" }\n```\n\n**Degraded case, same schema, no loss of addressability** — a `third-party-copyright` source with an OCR-only text layer stores `quote_sha256`, `first_8_words`, `page_printed` and `locator_precision: \"page\"` with `degradation_reason: \"OCR-LOW\"`, `redact_on_render: true`. The claim is still uniquely addressed, still joinable, still gate-checkable — it simply cannot be rendered verbatim.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Requirements for the new entry-creation plan\n\nNumbered, grouped, each with the evidence that motivates it. This is the direct input to writing the plan.\n\n### A. Source preparation\n\n**A1.** Derive the source inventory **from disk** in Phase 0 — `md5sum`, `pdfinfo`, first-page text extraction of title/author/year/venue — and diff it against any plan-supplied table, reporting phantoms and extras as **blocking** findings before any unit is assigned. *(`boredom:44-85` produced a phantom paper, a reversed byline, and two omissions that were the sole grounding for the plan's own debate axis; `boredom:92` asserted a 727-page proceedings volume was a single paper.)*\n\n**A2.** Every factual assertion a plan makes about a file (page count, identity, uniqueness, authorship, year) carries its **verification command and output inline**, or is marked UNVERIFIED with the verification assigned to Phase 0. *(same)*\n\n**A3.** Retain the de-dup/haystack rubric verbatim (md5 DROP / same-study MERGE with `dup-variant` / `>300pp` HAYSTACK with grep-locate and `-f/-l` re-extraction / `HAYSTACK-UNRESOLVED`), and persist dispositions with md5 evidence to the manifest. *(`TEMPLATE:57-67`; 23 duplicate groups across 288 corpus PDFs; two real salvages)*\n\n**A4.** **Source admissibility precondition.** Before authoring: distinct per-page text hashes, extracted-words-per-page floor, ligature-integrity probe (pypdfium2 fi/ff/fl dropout), expected-diacritic probe for the source's language, and citation completeness (author, venue, year, pagination anchor). Record `text_quality` per source. Quarantine failures with a remediation task; do not author around them. *(`ptf-01` shipped with an identical hash on all 11 pages and all verbatims UNVERIFIED; `riv-02` with an unverified venue; `ig-10-deep.json:425-430` documents the ligature damage; Uexküll's corrupted orthography is the variant that reaches runtime)*\n\n**A5.** **Rights tiering per source**, recorded in the source manifest: `own-work / public-domain / licensed / third-party-copyright`. *(`TEMPLATE:44` hardcodes one assumption for a template meant to process \"ANY folder\"; Aristotle, Equiano 1789, Radcliffe 1794, Austen 1811 and the user's own thesis were all suppressed under it)*\n\n**A6.** **Commit the normalized text projection** as an immutable artifact inside the entry: `<entry>/_source/<source_id>.txt` + sidecar `{tool, tool_version, exact_command, flags, source_sha256, text_sha256, extracted_at, page_map[]}`. Every locator names that artifact id. *(`TEMPLATE:138` sends it to a scratchpad; `vr-ped:239` observes the scratchpad does not survive a session and specifies it anyway; ~1,000 In-Game clause pointers are dead as a result)*\n\n**A7.** **Page-offset calibration, mandatory, multi-anchor, drift-tested.** ≥10 verified `(page_printed, page_pdf)` pairs spread across the document; assert monotonicity and affineness; record a piecewise map when it drifts; re-verify whenever `source_sha256` changes. *(Aristotle 33/34 records wrong by ≤47pp, bekker-index 101/188 off by >2; Rickert declared 20, drifts 18→15; the correct pattern already exists at `Uncomfortable Situations/_synthesis/us-literary-loci-concordance.json` `page_offset_rule` and in `Wendt/_synthesis/page-offset-verification.md`)*\n\n**A8.** **Per-source structural inventory as a Phase-1 artifact**: section list with page ranges, table/figure list, page count, word count. This is the denominator that makes coverage computable rather than asserted. *(no coverage gate is currently possible; Holmqvist 53pp yielded 0.19 readings/page vs Aho 3pp at 1.67 — an inverse density relation no count floor can see)*\n\n### B. Extraction and density\n\n**B1.** **The CLAIM is the unit of production; prose is a rendering of it.** State this before any phase. *(the source-as-atom design at `TEMPLATE:127-130` is the granularity ceiling)*\n\n**B2.** **Delete all prose word budgets.** Prose length is an output, not an input constraint. *(`TEMPLATE:153-154`; 17 of 18 band violations are overshoots — the measurable signature of analysts writing into prose what the schema could not hold)*\n\n**B3.** **Density floor expressed per 1,000 source words**, calibrated at **one record per 58–60 source words** (Dissertation 1/58 over 982 records; Veri(dis)similitude 262 addressable rows / 15,481 words = 1/59; the sandbox achieves 155–512 claims per article). Per-source floors: monograph ≥150, article ≥40, MA thesis ≥60. Compute the target from `A8`'s word count and record `claim_count_target` vs `claim_count_actual`. *(current: Boredom 1 per ~1,218 source words, ~21× coarser)*\n\n**B4.** **Coverage floor, not effort floor:** sections-with-≥1-claim / total sections = 1.0; pages-with-≥1-locus / total pages ≥ declared threshold. *(edge floors passed 55/55 while three units shipped zero readings)*\n\n**B5.** **Distribution gate:** no unit below 50% of the entry median claims-per-page. *(one under-extracted source currently hides inside a healthy aggregate)*\n\n**B6.** **Negative claims are records**, not a trailing prose line. *(`TEMPLATE:158` mandates `\"Not treated:\"`; bor-sec-30 names 8 explicitly-absent measures and bor-sec-13 names 3 absent constructs, none of which appear in any JSON array)*\n\n**B7.** **Windowed authoring protocol** for high-density production: id pre-allocation per window, deterministic window boundaries from `A8`'s section inventory, explicit merge step. *(at 50–500 records × 55 sources a single main-loop pass is 5,000–27,500 records; `TEMPLATE:167` requires main-loop authoring of the aggregate)*\n\n**B8.** **Migration is part of the plan, not a sequel.** Specify a deterministic lift for each existing shape: Dissertation `phase2-claims.json` (982, already schema-shaped) · VDS pipe table (157 rows with tier + disposition + anchor enum) · BT markdown table (108 rows + 299 fenced-JSON edges + 84 claim→tension back-refs) · Uexküll `Claim|Evidence type|Strength|Page ref` (107) · BCAP enumerated premises (150) · FCM (245 + ~1,100 locus-anchored prose claims + 2,090 quoted spans) · Boredom `readings[]` (2,924 sub-items, 2,012 of 2,258 dict-shaped already carrying a page locus) · Wendt `{text, locus}` (139) · Uncomfortable positions + 176 clause-level loci records · Aristotle (973 Bekker bullets, 2,323 loci) · In-Game (995 line anchors, resurrectable by one deterministic re-extraction) · RDR2 Playthrough (1,040 frame ids + 529 timestamps + 1,326 bullets) · VR Pedagogy (1,277 prose assertions vs 233 structured). Plus **promote the 4,961 existing span-anchored sandbox claims out of `tmp/`** (24 sources, 93.0% carrying char spans, 14,811 concept-mentions already linking them to ontology nodes with `provenance{bekker, chunk_id, char_start, char_end}`). *(This is the single largest available jump toward the goal and requires re-authoring nothing.)*\n\n### C. Schema and IDs\n\n**C1.** **Ship machine-checkable schema files as artifacts of the plan**, referenced by path: `claim.schema.json`, `clause.schema.json`, `edge.schema.json`, `locus.schema.json`, `tension.schema.json`, `term.schema.json`. **No `*.schema.json` exists anywhere in the repo today.** *(49 schema-violation defects)*\n\n**C2.** **One worked exemplar record per type**, schema-valid and reachable, shipped with the plan and handed to every agent. *(`TEMPLATE:212` points agents at a prose file as the quality bar)*\n\n**C3.** **Forbid bare strings in any array.** *(87 bare-string concepts, 146 interlocutors, 56 tensions, 57 sections in one entry)*\n\n**C4.** **Fix the case convention (snake_case) in the schema, not in prose.** *(54 `sampleN` vs 41 `sample_n` inside the one field set the plan did specify — in prose)*\n\n**C5.** **Full id grammar at every level, with worked examples,** globally unique across the entire `corpus/index/` tree: `<ENTRY>-<UNIT>-C<nnnn>` claims, `-CL<nnnnn>` clauses, `-S<nnn>` sections, `-T<nnn>` tensions, `-Q<nnn>` quotes, `-E<nnn>` edges. **Explicitly forbid unprefixed local counters.** *(42 colliding values across 8 units; `DA1`–`DA3` collide 8 ways)*\n\n**C6.** **IDs are content-addressed, not positional:** `entry_id + unit_id + sha256(claim_text)[0:8]`. Positional ids renumber on every insert. *(44 dangling-reference + 10 id-collision defects)*\n\n**C7.** **Ids are the ONLY join key.** Ban name-based merging; a same-name concept across entries becomes an explicit authored `sameAs` edge. *(the compiler merges on `name.lower()`, producing 20 fused rows with concatenated provenance; no compiled node carries an id at all)*\n\n**C8.** **Committed prefix and id registry** (prefix → entry → grammar → allocated ranges → status). Reserving the prefix is step 0. Collision fails the build. *(the `bor-` → `bex-` rename was unrecorded and `bor-` was subsequently taken by Boredom Secondary)*\n\n**C9.** **Every categorical field gets a closed enum stated inline in the plan**, with null illegal on `stance`, `support_tier`, `provenance`, `claim_kind`, `evidence_type`. Free-text nuance goes to a separate `note`. **Enums must be pairwise disjoint** and the validator must reject cross-contamination. *(`stance: \"FE\"` 22 times; `FAITHFUL-Elpidorou, p.4` smuggling a locus into the tag field — which was, note, plan-compliant given `boredom:33`'s own template)*\n\n**C10.** **Global versioned relation and type registry**, extensible only by a registered subtype declaring its parent, written back in the same commit. Gate: every relation string resolves. *(645 distinct relation values across 219 CSVs; edges from two entries cannot be unioned)*\n\n**C11.** **One canonical edge record, one physical format** at per-source and aggregate level, header stated verbatim in the plan, gated on exact equality: `edge_id, entry_id, subject_id, relation, object_id, domain, locators[], provenance, support_tier, confidence, deriving_unit, note`. Typed endpoints — record ids, never display strings. *(four incompatible headers; 119 rows with `§4`/`n.8`/`Intro` as subject; and a canonical schema four months older already existed at `scripts/normalize-edges.py` and was never cited)*\n\n**C12.** **One authoritative store per layer; every `.md` is GENERATED** by a committed script and gated on byte-reproducibility. Kill the hand-authored `{md,json}` twin pattern. *(`TEMPLATE:114, :176-177`; 36 canonical positions lost to JSON files the compiler never opens; Uncomfortable's two disjoint concept registries)*\n\n**C13.** **Stamp `schema_version` into every artifact.** *(only Dissertation does; nothing else can be migrated safely)*\n\n**C14.** **`surface_form` is a first-class indexed field** alongside the normalized label. *(`TEMPLATE:81-88` normalises the source's own term into a free-text note)*\n\n**C15.** **UTF-8 NFC normalisation rule + one canonical orthography per lemma with `variants[]`;** a checker flags any two lemmas differing only by normalisation or mojibake. **Forbid encoding fallbacks in the loader** — a decode failure is a hard error, not silent latin-1. *(Uexküll's four orthographies; the corrupted one wins)*\n\n### D. Provenance and verification\n\n**D1.** **`provenance` is a required enum field on every record**, not a prose convention. *(currently 201 of 463 Boredom readings carry null; VR Pedagogy has 1,136 prose tokens vs 233 fields)*\n\n**D2.** **`derivation` on every record** (`agent-read / self-authored / inferred / script-derived`), with a gate on the self-authored fraction. **Forbid the orchestrator from self-authoring a unit it has not read**; re-dispatch to a fresh agent with the source. *(`TEMPLATE:208-210`)*\n\n**D3.** **Quotation is machine-verified, not length-limited.** Every quoted span at any length is stored as `{quote_id, doc_id, char_start, char_end, exact_text, sha256}` extracted from the committed text layer, never typed by an agent. **Ban quotation marks in hand-typed prose**; quotations are interpolated by id (`scripts/substitute-quote-ids.py` already exists and exits 1 on unknown ids — wire it). Gate: re-slice the committed text at the recorded offsets and assert byte equality. *(≥4 fabricated spans shipped in `ped-sec-29` under FE tags, all inside the 12-word allowance)*\n\n**D4.** **Rights-tiered storage/display split.** Store the exact span for every tier; the word ceiling applies only to **rendered output** and only for restricted tiers, with `redact_on_render` on the record. **Forbid the FE tag on any sentence containing an unverified quoted span.** *(`TEMPLATE:44`; the current rule forced In-Game to truncate canonical definitions to 24/23/20 words and Uncomfortable to suppress the clause entirely)*\n\n**D5.** **Persist retrieval provenance, never assert it.** Every quotation record carries `{doc_id, chunk_id, page, bbox[x0,y0,x1,y1], char_span, sim, mode, snapshot_id, run_timestamp}` exactly as `archon evidence find --mode exact` returns them. **Ban the token `bbox ✓` as evidence.** Gate: numeric-bbox coverage = 100%. *(45+ ticks recorded across three entries; zero coordinates stored — the clause-level address existed at authoring time in every one of those 22 loci and was thrown away)*\n\n**D6.** **Locator resolvability gate:** ≥3 randomly sampled loci per source verified by string-matching the cited text on the mapped page; every char span resolves inside the committed text; every recorded page resolves inside the document's real range. *(loci are currently \"carried\", never resolved)*\n\n**D7.** **Bibliographic verification against the title page / DOI / copyright line**, recording the version-of-record year, gated `verified_bibliography: true`. **Decouple storage handles from bibliographic facts** — folders and filenames use the opaque id alone. **Gate that no unresolved corrections file exists at sign-off.** *(the `Colin`/Barrett freeze is permanent; `citation-corrections-2026-07-16.md` documents four corrections still unapplied)*\n\n**D8.** **Record per-unit build provenance** in the manifest: agent id, model, retries, self-authored flag, cost. **Independent second-reader verification on a stated sample fraction with a stated pass threshold.** *(no build provenance is recorded anywhere)*\n\n### E. Edges and connection\n\n**E1.** **Invert the edge default.** Every relation an author can state in prose MUST be emitted as a typed edge; omission requires a recorded rationale. *(cross-entry references currently live in prose and reach nothing)*\n\n**E2.** **Referential integrity is a hard gate.** Every `subject_id`/`object_id` resolves to an existing record in this entry or a registered sibling. Unresolvable = 0, or a typed row in the open-items file with a named blocking dependency. **Forbid authoring any edge whose target entry does not exist**; route intent to `pending-bridges.json`. *(`grounds-measure` 0/37; `bridges-to-part-iii` 0/128; `vr-ped:20,:132` explicitly authorised 24 edges to a never-built anchor)*\n\n**E3.** **Enumerate the literal target id list inline for every cross-entry relation,** or ship the command that generates it; where the target does not yet exist, use reserved placeholder ids from a declared namespace, never free text. *(`boredom:24` → 100% resolution; prose description → 0%)*\n\n**E4.** **Evidence-preserving merge, implemented as a committed script.** Merge on `(subject_id, relation, object_id)` and **UNION the locator sets**; emit `{rows_in, rows_out, loci_in, loci_preserved, dropped_ids[], drop_reason_histogram}`; **fail when `loci_preserved < loci_in`** or when any `drop_reason` is `unknown`. Better still: never dedup on content at all — concatenate on `edge_id` and report near-duplicates for human resolution. **Gate `count(global) == sum(count(per-unit))` as exact equality.** *(18 + 2 evidence rows destroyed; the count-mismatch class is 66 of 551)*\n\n**E5.** **Bridges require two resolved endpoints or they do not exist:** `{bridge_id, source_entry_id, source_node_id, target_entry_id, target_node_id, bridge_text (min length), evidence_locus_source, evidence_locus_target, state}`. Empty endpoint = hard failure. *(42 of 72 live hooks have an empty `targetConcept`; `cross-author-utils.ts:473-474` makes `t.includes('')` always true, so all 42 are candidates for every topic; 525 of 552 sandbox bridge candidates were generated against an empty anchor and 85% came back \"unrelated\", versus 25 of 27 usable from well-formed anchors — a 6× yield difference)*\n\n**E6.** **Floor source-derived records; CAP interpretive ones.** `P`-tagged ≤ 0.15 × (`FE` + `FAITHFUL`). *(`vr-ped:184,:220` mandate a *minimum* of the project's own speculation per unit; 117 speculative edges = 10.4% of the store)*\n\n**E7.** **Separate data caps from render caps, explicitly.** No cap on cross-entry edges, canonical nodes, concordance cells or claim records in the store; caps apply only to a generated view, produced by filtering on tier/centrality. *(`TEMPLATE:185`'s ≤25 cap forced strand-level aggregation that deleted 117 unit-level edges into 8 integer labels)*\n\n**E8.** **Every matrix/concordance/graph is a GENERATED VIEW over records**, never hand- or join-built. Every cell-source assertion resolves to exactly one `claim_id` and carries direction, effect size (or null), and provenance. **Explicitly forbid mechanical co-occurrence derivation by name** — it is the cheapest way to pass a coverage gate. Gate: `unbacked_assertions == 0`. *(85–91% of VR Pedagogy's concordance assertions are co-occurrence artifacts)*\n\n**E9.** **Build a reverse-reference index at compile time** (record id → every file citing it) and make correction transactional: changing a record lists dependents and fails until each is updated or waived. *(a superseded VLE figure has 12 live copies in a sibling entry; 22 live \"not yet built\" assertions about an entry built 2026-07-16)*\n\n### F. Weakness and tension encoding\n\n**F1.** **`support_tier` is required on every claim**, using the 8-tier taxonomy. This is the mechanism by which \"every weakness\" becomes queryable: T4/T5/T6/T7 are the weaknesses, machine-selectable. *(Dissertation: 477 T3, 41 T4, 71 T5, 12 T6, 22 T7 over 982 records — the only working instance in the corpus)*\n\n**F2.** **Pair `flag_present` with the quoted hedge** (`flag_text`). *(this is what makes a T3 rating auditable rather than asserted)*\n\n**F3.** **Tensions get a typed record and the compiler's exact key names.** One shape subsuming all eight observed on disk: `{tension_id, entry_id, endpoint_a{node_id,label}, endpoint_b{node_id,label}, relation, directed, evidence_locus_a, evidence_locus_b, description, unit_ids[], claim_ids[], staged_by_sources: bool}`. Must cover `node_a/node_b`, `nodeA/nodeB/type`, `wendt_position/against`, `pole_A/pole_B`, `tension_id/label/supporting_units`, `pentad_terms_involved`, and the FCM `locus_a/locus_b` variant. *(55 records lost; 4 of 11 files yield zero)*\n\n**F4.** **Contested readings are typed records at ENTRY scope, re-based on named external interlocutors**, not a prose list and not a cross-source-only artifact. *(VR CR-01/CR-03 contest Short et al. 1976 and the SSQ — neither a cluster unit; 18 shipped against a stated band of 8–12, unflagged, because the artifact has no format)*\n\n**F5.** **Replace count targets on relational discoveries with coverage + evidence gates.** Every recorded disagreement cites ≥2 distinct records with resolvable loci on opposing sides and carries `staged_by_sources`; report analyst-constructed axes separately and never gate on the total. *(VR DA-07 and DA-08 reference exactly one unit each; Boredom flags 3 of 11 axes `constructedByCluster`)*\n\n**F6.** **`implicit_citations_needed[]` is a required array** — the index must name the citation the prose is *missing*, not only what it has. *(Dissertation 982/982; nothing else in the corpus does this)*\n\n**F7.** **`volatility` + `disposition` on every claim.** *(VDS: a vocabulary change becomes a work queue instead of silent rot; the only actionable-during-drafting fields in the corpus)*\n\n### G. Gates\n\n**G1.** **Every gate is a named committed executable with a numeric threshold and an exit code.** Required checkers, all of which must exist **before** authoring begins: `check-schema`, `check-ids` (uniqueness + cross-ref resolution), `check-loci` (resolution through the declared offset map), `check-projection` (re-run extraction, compare sha256), `check-density`, `check-coverage`, `check-registration` (non-zero compiled contribution per layer), `check-quotes` (span fidelity + rights class), `check-lemmas` (non-Latin assertion on lemma fields + NFC), `check-mermaid` (`mmdc`, non-zero exit if absent), `check-debates`, `check-dedup` (loci preserved), `emit-gates`. **A gate whose executable is missing must FAIL, not pass by narration.** *(`TEMPLATE:199,:228` name a verbatim detector that does not exist)*\n\n**G2.** **Never name a tool the plan does not ship.** *(same)*\n\n**G3.** **Gate results are artifacts:** `_audit/gates.json` — one object per gate `{gate_id, scope, threshold_expr, threshold_value, measured, verdict (PASS/FAIL/SKIPPED-N1/NA-BY-CONSTRUCTION), checker, checker_version, measured_at, input_sha256, evidence_path}` — plus `_audit/metrics.json` and a rendered report. Registration is conditional on zero FAILs. **Preserve RDR2's \"Gates NOT fully met (reported honestly)\" as a required section.** *(2 of 27 entries have a report; 1 has metrics)*\n\n**G4.** **Never write a derived constant into a gate.** Every threshold is an expression over a value the checker reads from the manifest at check time. **Delete \"do not re-open\" phrasing** from any decision a later phase can invalidate, and add an explicit scope-change procedure: any change to N re-runs the gate script and requires fresh sign-off. *(`vr-ped:213,:216` froze N=23 and 276 while N drifted to 34)*\n\n**G5.** **Separate producer from judge structurally.** Authoring agents may not write gate results. *(every surviving gate record in the corpus is self-attestation embedded inside the artifact it judges)*\n\n**G6.** **Replace \"compiler runs clean\" with validate-then-load that exits non-zero.** Assertions: manifest-declared count per record type == loaded count; zero-yield for a registered source is a hard failure; every rejected record is written to a rejects file with a reason; gate on the rejects file being empty and on `compiler_warnings == 0`. *(`main()` cannot fail; 55 records discarded with 0 warnings)*\n\n**G7.** **Never gate on a marker; gate on the loader's output.** Run the loader, read back the count, and round-trip a named spot-check record field-for-field. *(the `## 3A` gate is uncorrelated with what the parser does; the count gate certified 60 nodes while 19 were corrupted)*\n\n**G8.** **Registration contract test as a Phase-0 gate.** Compile a committed fixture, assert the compiled output exactly equals an expected node list; re-run on the real entry asserting (a) compiled count == authored count, (b) every compiled name string-equals its authored heading, (c) `greek`/`transliteration` empty for non-classical entries, (d) `canonicalTerms` contributed by this entry minus authored names == ∅. *(19 corrupted nodes; `technological` and `control` in the global greedy-match list)*\n\n**G9.** **Canonical-term admission gate.** A term enters the global list only if declared in a per-entry terms file, exceeds a minimum length, and is not a bare common English word (stoplist). Print the full diff of terms this entry adds, for sign-off at G1. *(1,722 terms currently including whole sentences and bare words)*\n\n**G10.** **Every gate is scope-tagged RECORD / ENTRY / GROUP with a declared minimum N,** and the checker emits `NA-BY-CONSTRUCTION` rather than a missing artifact below the minimum. **N=1 is the default path.** Per-source intrinsic gates, all meaningful at N=1: records per 1,000 source words · schema-validity rate = 1.0 · id-uniqueness = 1.0 · enum-conformance = 1.0 · locator-resolution rate = 1.0 · quote-verification rate = 1.0 · char-span coverage ≥ 0.90 (the sandbox already achieves 0.930) with a `match_ratio` floor (its minimum is 0.083 against a median of 1.000) · section coverage = 1.0 · endpoint-resolution rate = 1.0 · unbacked assertions = 0 · reachability ≥ 0.95 · unresolved `******` = 0 · self-authored fraction ≤ threshold. Move debates, intra-cluster citation network and the scholarly-evolution arc to a GROUP layer with minimum membership ≥5. **Skipping a GROUP gate is a pass.** *(3 gates genuinely collapse; 1 is unsatisfiable by construction; `max(10, N/4)` taught executors to reinterpret rather than fail)*\n\n**G11.** **Reachability gate:** `reachable_records / authored_records ≥ 0.95`, computed by a script that loads the compiled artifact and resolves authored ids, plus a per-artifact table `records_on_disk vs records_in_compiled_index`. **No artifact ships at 0% reachability** without a signed waiver naming the future loader. *(VR Pedagogy scores 0.046)*\n\n**G12.** **File-manifest gate.** Ship `manifest.expected.json` as data; gate on set equality with the on-disk tree, both directions. *(`units/` empty in both template-lineage entries; four artifacts specified-but-absent in Boredom)*\n\n**G13.** **Cross-artifact numeric consistency gate.** Scan every `.md`/`.json` in the entry for count claims and fail on any that disagrees with the one authoritative register. Mark superseded phase artifacts SUPERSEDED with a pointer. *(`phase0-overview.md` permanently declares 46 against a manifest of 55; BCAP §3B contradicts its companion CSV in every line)*\n\n**G14.** **Post-build corpus-wide invariant sweep** after any entry is created or renamed: grep the whole index for assertions about its prior state (`not yet built`, `****** UNVERIFIED`, superseded prefixes, superseded counts) and fail on any hit. *(22 live hits for the Boredom anchor; 12 for the superseded VLE figure)*\n\n**G15.** **Duplicate-content gate:** normalised shingle overlap between any two unit files above threshold fails the build, replacing prose \"no duplication\" rules. *(three files assert non-duplication that a fourth falsifies inside one entry)*\n\n**G16.** **\"Gates deferred\" is prohibited.** A build with deferred gates is a draft and must not register. *(VLE's manifest records `\"gates deferred to post-run review\"`; the review never happened and 100% of what VLE serves to runtime is stale)*\n\n**G17.** **Preserve backups + G0 + G1 + no-commit-before-G1**, with the backup paths named and their existence and timestamp ordering asserted by the gate script. **G1 reviews `gates.json`, the per-layer compiled-contribution delta, a checker-selected random sample of k records with their loci actually opened and resolved, the canonical-term diff, and the open-items list** — not one author-chosen unit trio (1.8% of a 55-unit build). *(`TEMPLATE:229`; Boredom's `.backups/` contains neither file the plan names)*\n\n### H. Orchestration\n\n**H1.** **Per-unit conformance validation on agent return**, not a batch existence check: schema-validate, assert record floors, assert enum membership, assert every `quote_id` verifies against the committed text, assert no placeholder strings. Re-dispatch failures to a fresh agent **with the source**. Emit a per-unit pass/fail row into the gates report. *(all 34 VR folders passed the existence check; the entry still drew 36 defects)*\n\n**H2.** **Synthesis is DERIVED by a committed script, not authored.** Per-source records are complete and valid independently; aggregation is re-runnable and reports `rows_in/rows_out/rejects`; any model-authored interpretive layer operates over the script's output, is sharded by axis with a declared merge order, and cites derived record ids. **Re-run the aggregation from scratch at the end and byte-compare.** *(`TEMPLATE:167`; strain already visible at 2,924 sub-items — a dropped cell schema and 18 lost tuples)*\n\n**H3.** **Deferrals are first-class typed records:** `_audit/deferred.json` `{deferral_id, what, blocking_dependency, resolution_procedure, on_clear_actions[exact files to rewrite], owner, review_date, created_at}`. A gate **fails** any entry whose deferral names a dependency that now exists. Corpus-wide sweep whenever a new entry lands. *(`boredom:274-275`; 37 edges + 12 mappings still unresolved 13 days after the blocker cleared; a deferred folder rename never executed)*\n\n**H4.** **Every `****** UNVERIFIED:` is a row in the open-items file** with the exact assertion that closes it. Entry status gates on the file being empty. *(nothing currently converts, tracks or fails on a placeholder; the concordance gate's own escape clause passes them)*\n\n**H5.** **Any script producing index-bound aggregates writes to a tracked, schema-validated file inside the entry.** Forbid gitignoring derived anonymised index content. *(`scripts/boredom-o9/.gitignore` excludes `out/`; the only significant statistical finding this dataset has produced — pupil dilation Boring < Clinical, all 8 subjects, p=0.008 — is nowhere in `corpus/index/`)*\n\n**H6.** **Verified facts are entry content, not plan content.** Any fact a plan verifies (schema, offset, cell inventory, measured value) is written into the entry with its verification method and locus **at the moment of verification**, before any subsequent phase runs. **Plan supersession requires a SUPERSEDED-BY banner plus a fact-migration checklist** enumerating every verified fact and its destination or explicit discard rationale. *(v2's byte-verified 12-column schema, 24-cell table, ~2.99 Hz cadence measurement and 4-channel S05 result are stranded in a plan file, while the built entry states \"120 Hz\" for the same channel)*\n\n**H7.** **One plan per entry, versioned**, with `governing_plan` + `plan_version` + `plan_sha` written into the entry manifest. **Forbid entry creation from a phase report.** *(three of five thin entries were built from `new-media-presence-ingestion-phase1-report-2026-07-20.md`, which has no gates section, no acceptance criteria and no definition of done; three Boredom plans exist, two describing an entry never built, none referenced from the entry)*\n\n**H8.** **Entry-profile declaration before building**, from a fixed set with different floors and required artifacts: `PRIMARY-DATASET` (record per measurement cell + per derived metric) · `MONOGRAPH` · `ARTICLE` (N=1 default) · `ARTICLE-CLUSTER` · `SMALL-PAIR` (N≤3: no cross-source statistics, full per-source extraction, outbound edges mandatory) · `OWN-PROSE`. Record it in the manifest; select thresholds from it. *(a 2-source rhetoric pair, a 4-source theory cluster and a 92 GB instrumented dataset all converged on the same 7–10 node ontology-only shape)*\n\n**H9.** **Consent and use-restriction modelled per record (`use_scope`), never as an entry-wide content ceiling.** *(O-10 permanently capped the Boredom Experiment at ~8 assertions for a 168-cell instrument)*\n\n**H10.** **Preserve `planCorrections` with a fixed schema** `{issue, files, evidence[] (command + output), resolution, residual}`, and require the executor to record plan contradictions **without editing the plan**. *(correction #7 is the single best piece of process behaviour in the corpus)*\n\n**H11.** **Preserve \"refuse and escalate\" as a sanctioned agent outcome**, distinct from the no-stall doctrine. *(the `bor-sec-18` refusal)*\n\n**H12.** **Self-consistency read of the plan itself as a pre-execution step;** any count stated in prose must be derivable from the enumeration it introduces. *(`boredom:41` \"Six strands\" followed by seven; `boredom:208` vs `:261` contradicting each other on the bridge obligation)*\n\n**H13.** **Idempotency and growth contract:** what a second execution over an existing entry does; how new records append without renumbering; how ids are reserved; how a re-extracted source invalidates and re-anchors dependents; how a rebuild diff is produced. **Single-run-of-record rule** for entries carrying multiple run histories. *(undefined everywhere; `Dissertation` carries two identical full run-histories with no rule for which counts)*\n\n**H14.** **State the budget and cost model up front.** Reference points: $1.33/paper and ~$0.005/claim for claim extraction ($20 → 3,776 claims from 15 papers); ~$0.30/drafting run. A 27-entry claim-level pass is on the order of $40–80 for extraction plus harness runs. *(no plan states one; scope is currently set by guesswork)*\n\n### I. Wiring and runtime\n\n**I1.** **Define the runtime record contract and the loader FIRST**, before any authoring instruction. **Nothing may be mandated as a deliverable unless a named loader reads it.** *(the inversion is the root cause of D1)*\n\n**I2.** **Open the plan with a REACHABILITY CONTRACT derived by reading the loader at execution time:** a table of `(artifact path → reader file:function → runtime destination)`, plus the command that prints, for a named entry, exactly which paths the compiler opens — and require the executing agent to **run it and paste the output** into the gates report. Cite compiler behaviour by **function name plus a reproduction command, never by line number**. *(the anchor plan cited \"verified `compile-corpus-index.py` L1197–1207\", wrong branch, fallback direction stated backwards)*\n\n**I3.** **Every commissioned artifact names its reader on the same line**, or the plan commissions the reader as a deliverable, or the artifact is dropped. **Classify every file in the entry READ-BY-LOADER / AGENT-READ-BY-PATH / HUMAN-ONLY** in a committed `_synthesis/reachability.json`. *(Note: a binary read-by-loader/human-only partition is wrong — drafting agents genuinely read unit `.md` files by path under the \"corpus/index FIRST\" discipline. Use the three-way classification, and gate on per-record round-trip, **not** on a byte fraction, which is gameable by bloating `definition` text.)*\n\n**I4.** **Registration is data-driven and happens at entry CREATION.** Each entry declares itself in a committed `entry.json` at a conventional path (`{entry_id, profile, adapter, schema_version, governing_plan, plan_sha, expected_record_counts}`); the loader discovers entries by glob. **Delete the hand-edited `TEXT_DIRS` dict.** A stub entry registers on day one and grows — an unfinished entry is visible-and-empty, never invisible. *(8 of 27 entries unregistered for want of a dict line, including the two richest claim assets; under a ~265-single-source-entry direction this is 265 manual edits with a demonstrated 30% forget rate)*\n\n**I5.** **Make the index path injectable in the live tree** — honour `CORPUS_INDEX_PATH` in `jsonl-loaders.ts:198-200` and stop ignoring `options.indexPath` in `corpus-index-provider.ts:73-77`. **~20 LOC, and the precondition for every future measurement.** The sandbox fork already implements it and the patch was never merged. *(without it no A/B arm can run without forking `src` again)*\n\n**I6.** **Emit what the index contributed:** wire `corpusIndexContributions {ontologyNodesUsed, hooksInjected, tensionEdgesUsed, claimsUsed}` and `injectedBridges[]` into recorded run JSON. The code paths exist (`write-pipeline-orchestrator.ts:833-860`, `cli.ts:1616`) and appear in **0** of the recorded run outputs, so no run on record can show whether the index touched the prompt at all.\n\n**I7.** **Two-stage retrieval, so claim count never competes with concept count:** concepts select a candidate set, claims are retrieved within it; per-source quota so a dense source cannot crowd out a sparse one; length-normalised scoring; claim budget **additive** to the concept budget. Gate on **source-coverage retention ≥ baseline**. *(the measured penalty for skipping this is quality 0.794→0.789 with six named authors dropping out of the prose at 4.3× index scale — the metric that caught it was source coverage, not quality score)*\n\n**I8.** **Embed at claim granularity from v1;** concept vectors are derived centroids. *(one vector per concept reproduces the ceiling in the vector layer)*\n\n**I9.** **Ship a QUERY SURFACE as a named deliverable with acceptance tests:** given a topic, return top-k claim records with spans, concept ids and source. *(zero references to any claim store across `src/` and `scripts/`; an index nobody can query cannot improve drafting)*\n\n**I10.** **Every phase ends with records reaching runtime, and that number strictly increases.** No all-or-nothing cutover; land new record types alongside the existing compiled index before any storage migration; keep rollback. *(the migration spec's terminal-phase parity gate delays all user-visible value to the end)*\n\n**I11.** **Forbid new index artifacts under `tmp/`**, and promote what is already there. *(the 4,961 span-anchored claims; `tmp/Dissertation/...` is referenced as canonical from 5 places inside a committed entry)*\n\n**I12.** **Fix the bridge selector before any derivative generation:** filter empty endpoints before scoring; if nothing scores > 0, emit no MANDATORY block rather than degrading to `\"<-> ? ()\"`; never label an INTERP-tagged record \"verified\". *(`cross-author-utils.ts:473-474`; simulated over 6 realistic dissertation topics, 4 of 6 select an empty-target hook under a MUST-cite directive labelled \"verified, high-confidence\" — an anti-gate that compels fabrication)*\n\n**I13.** **Pin the evaluation config in version control with a recorded SHA** (prompt list, source list, seeds, arm definitions), following the existing `ARTIFACT-MANIFEST.json` frozen-suite pattern. **Keep the A/B process firewall** (draft fully in one condition before opening the other index) — the best methodological feature in the evaluation lineage. **Run the paired arm that needs no new authoring first:** seven sources already exist in both representations (Caston 1995, Frede 1992, Nussbaum 1985, O'Gorman 2005, Papachristou 2013, White 1985, Bowin 2017), ~72 runs at ~$0.30 each.\n\n---\n\n### The single sentence the new plan must open with\n\n> The atom of this index is the **claim**, addressed to the **clause**, stored as a validated record against a committed hashed text projection; every artifact this plan commissions is either an input to a named loader or a generated rendering of the record store, and every gate is an executable that writes its result to disk."
  },
